{
  "raw": {
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34693": {
      "title": "Tenured/Tenure-Track Professor in Law and Emerging Technologies",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Tenured/Tenure-Track Professor in Law and Emerging Technologies Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Tenured/Tenure-Track Professor in Law and Emerging Technologies Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Tenured/Tenure-Track Professor in Law and Emerging Technologies Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Maurer School of Law in Bloomington is seeking outstanding lateral tenured or tenure-track applicants in the regulation of artificial intelligence, robotics, and other emerging technologies. The position is part of Indiana University’s Faculty 100 (F100) initiative. The initiative is a campus-wide investment to recruit 100 new tenured/tenure-track faculty whose work strengthens IU’s research capacity in strategically important and rapidly growing areas. IU Bloomington has significant cross-campus strength in technology, informatics, business, labor, public affairs, ethics, and social science. The strongest candidate would be a scholar with a record or emerging agenda in one or more of the following areas: law and artificial intelligence, responsible AI, robotics, workforce transformation, human-centered technology, public-sector innovation, and technology’s social impacts. A law scholar in this area could contribute regulatory analysis, institutional design, and policy-relevant research pertaining to labor-market governance, tax and public-finance analysis, law and political economy, and/or normative frameworks for evaluating the distributional effects of technological change. We encourage applications from scholars who apply interdisciplinary perspectives and share important research overlap with current IUB scholars, while also offering new dimensions that will expand and strengthen the IU’s broader AI and emerging technologies research program. Features of the Maurer School of Law include: A highly collegial and productive faculty that is committed to retaining and expanding its community of scholars. Integration with a major research university, including cross-disciplinary collaborations with the Kelley School of Business; Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies; Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering; Ostrom Workshop in Political Theory and Policy Analysis; and the Paul H. O’Neill School of Public and Environmental Affairs, among others. Excellent and ambitious JD, LLM , and SJD students with strong entering credentials. A three-course teaching load, small average class sizes, generous support for research conference travel, and an excellent student-faculty ratio. Located on one of the nation’s most beautiful campuses in a vibrant Big Ten college town, and home to the world-renowned IU Jacobs School of Music, which presents between 1,100 and 1,400 performances and musical events per year. The candidate will have an expected start date of August 1, 2027 . Interested candidates should submit a CV and a letter summarizing their professional experience and future career goals in the areas of scholarship, teaching, and service. Additional materials may be requested during advanced stages of the evaluative process. Please submit these application materials to https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34180 . To be given fullest consideration, applications should be received no later than September 15, 2026 ; however, the search will remain open until the positions are filled. Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN., IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities while fostering a culturally diverse campus environment; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ Master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications include a distinguished academic background and a record of excellence in both scholarship and teaching, as well as a J.D., Ph.D., or comparable degree. Department Contact for Questions Questions regarding the position or application process can be directed to Professor Asaf Lubin, Chair, F100 Initiative Hiring Committee, at lawappts@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 09/15/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101654-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34692": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor Position in Economics",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Associate or Full Professor Position in Economics Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Associate or Full Professor Position in Economics Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Please submit: · Cover letter summarizing your qualifications and interest · Current CV · Research sample · Contact information for references (six references will be solicited from finalists) Posting Details Position Details Title Associate or Full Professor Position in Economics Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Economics Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington invites applications for an Elmus Wicker Chair position at the rank of associate or full professor in the Department of Economics. The 10-month appointment would ideally start August 1, 2027; an earlier or later start date is negotiable. We especially encourage candidates in Macroeconomics, Applied Microeconomics, Experimental Economics, Econometrics, and International Economics. Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. https://policies.iu.edu/policies/ua-01-non-discrimination/index.html Basic Qualifications Candidates must have a Ph.D., established research leadership, and the capacity for high-quality undergraduate and graduate teaching. Department Contact for Questions Questions: Erin Kirchhofer, (812) 855-2990, econadmn@indiana.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Please submit: · Cover letter summarizing your qualifications and interest · Current CV · Research sample · Contact information for references (six references will be solicited from finalists) For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101725-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Letter of Reference 4 Letter of Reference 5 Letter of Reference 6 Research Paper 1 List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34691": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Clinical Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Clinical Assistant Professor Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Required Application Materials – Please include all of the following : 1. Cover Letter: including explanation of why you are interested in this position and how your training and experience make you a good fit 2. CV 3. Graduate School Transcript (unofficial is sufficient) 4. Teaching Statement: including explanation of your teaching philosophy, examples of pedagogical strategies, and statement on how these relate to a clinical science curriculum 5. References: name, title, and contact information for three professional references OPTIONAL Application Materials – You may choose to include any or none of the following: 1. Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness: e.g., course evaluations; peer teaching evaluation; formal course observation, etc. 2. Example Syllabus 3. Example Course Materials: e.g., representative example lecture slides; lecture recording; and/or class assignments 4. Research Statement 5. Example Publication Application Deadline: For best consideration please submit your application by December 1, 2026. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. How to Apply: applicants should apply online at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34662 Posting Details Position Details Title Clinical Assistant Professor Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Psychological & Brain Sciences Location Bloomington Position Summary The Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences at Indiana University, Bloomington ( https://psych.indiana.edu/ ), invites applications for a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure-track position at the level of Clinical Assistant Professor to begin August 1, 2027. The qualified candidate will contribute to a new, highly innovative, and rigorous Bachelor of Science degree program in Clinical Psychological Science ( see: https://psych.indiana.edu/undergraduate/clinical-psych-bs.html ). This rapidly growing major is the first of its kind in the country and provides undergraduates with classroom and practicum-based training in experimental psychopathology and evidence-based assessment, intervention, dissemination, and implementation following a clinical science training model ( see: https://psych.indiana.edu/news-events/news/2025/clinical-science-major.html ). Job duties consist primarily of undergraduate teaching and may involve supervision of applied clinical experiences (e.g., internships & practica at local mental health and community-based organizations). We seek an individual with experience or ability to teach Research Methods in Clinical Science, Psychological Assessment and Testing, Abnormal Psychology, or evidence-based clinical interventions courses on disorders and topics within the candidate’s primary area of specialization. Candidates should be committed to a career of excellence in teaching and service, including coordinating degree requirements for the major, advising undergraduate students in academic and professional pursuits, and serving on departmental committees (e.g., student awards, undergraduate curricular planning). This will be a full-time non-tenure track, faculty appointment beginning with a 3-year renewable appointment, with promotion opportunities to Associate Clinical Professor and then Full Clinical Professor, based on demonstrated excellence in teaching and/or service. About Bloomington: Bloomington, Indiana is a university town with high quality of life and low cost of living. Bloomington is within a one-hour drive of Indianapolis and a two-hour drive of two other major metropolitan centers and four-hour drive of several others. IU Bloomington also has competitive entry-level faculty salaries. The campus is home to many thriving affinity groups and offers an exceptional selection of cultural, educational, and recreational opportunities. Here ( https://psych.indiana.edu/about/employment/faculty-hiring/index.html ), you will find contact information for a range of people with knowledge of the hiring process, as well as department, campus, and general life in Bloomington, who have volunteered to be search advocates and are not on the search committee. If you have questions that you may not feel comfortable bringing to the department chair or the members of the search committee, we encourage you to reach out to these faculty. Basic Qualifications Minimum qualifications are a Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology or a closely related discipline (e.g., Counseling, School Psychology) at the time of the appointment August 1, 2027 and undergraduate teaching experience. Department Contact for Questions Queries can be sent to Dr. Lorenzo Lorenzo-Luaces, Search Committee Chair, ATTN : Clinical Science Search, Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences, 1101 E. 10th Street, Bloomington, IN 47405-7007 or dcspbs@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Required Application Materials – Please include all of the following : 1. Cover Letter: including explanation of why you are interested in this position and how your training and experience make you a good fit 2. CV 3. Graduate School Transcript (unofficial is sufficient) 4. Teaching Statement: including explanation of your teaching philosophy, examples of pedagogical strategies, and statement on how these relate to a clinical science curriculum 5. References: name, title, and contact information for three professional references OPTIONAL Application Materials – You may choose to include any or none of the following: 1. Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness: e.g., course evaluations; peer teaching evaluation; formal course observation, etc. 2. Example Syllabus 3. Example Course Materials: e.g., representative example lecture slides; lecture recording; and/or class assignments 4. Research Statement 5. Example Publication Application Deadline: For best consideration please submit your application by December 1, 2026. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. How to Apply: applicants should apply online at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34662 For Best Consideration Date 12/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101740-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy List Of References Transcript Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Ability Other Publication 1 Sample Syllabus Statement of Research and Teaching Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34690": {
      "title": "Assistant Scientist - AI-Enabled Immune Digital Twin Workflows, Data Assimilation, and Ensemble Updating",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Scientist - AI-Enabled Immune Digital Twin Workflows, Data Assimilation, and Ensemble Updating Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Scientist - AI-Enabled Immune Digital Twin Workflows, Data Assimilation, and Ensemble Updating Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Scientist - AI-Enabled Immune Digital Twin Workflows, Data Assimilation, and Ensemble Updating Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Intelligent Systems Engineering Location Bloomington Position Summary Your primary duties will be to build reproducible, testable, sequential data-assimilating digital twin workflows under the direction of Dr. James A. Glazier. You will implement patient-specific forecasting and rebasing pipelines, design anomaly-detection and residual-monitoring logic, infer unobserved state parameters, manage complex model ensemble interfaces, and coordinate computational infrastructure with national consortium collaborators. 60% Digital Twin Workflows & Data Assimilation: Develop Python workflows for short-horizon forecasting and patient-specific rebasing; implement data-assimilation methods (Kalman/Bayesian updating); design anomaly detection and missing-information inference logic. 40% Software Engineering & Integration: Build reproducible computational packages(CI/CD, containers, testing); manage ensemble interfaces; integrate workflows with external consortium platforms (Vivarium, QSP ); write technical publications. Basic Qualifications Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in quantitative, computational, or biomedical discipline. Programming proficiency in Python, Julia, R, or MATLAB ; background in mechanistic modeling ( ODE /dynamical systems, QSP , or agent-based); familiarity with inflammation, cytokine signaling, sepsis, or critical care biology. One year of successful postdoctoral research experience. Department Contact for Questions Please contact Professor James Glazier at glazier@iu.edu with questions regarding the position. Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank 100,000/Assistant Scientist Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 11/02/2026 Expected Start Date Posting Number IU-101733-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
