    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34686": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor of Political Science – Quantitative Methods for Social Science",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Open Rank Professor of Political Science – Quantitative Methods for Social Science Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Open Rank Professor of Political Science – Quantitative Methods for Social Science Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All candidates should submit: (1) a cover letter describing research completed and planned; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a research statement; (4) two writing samples; (5) a teaching portfolio with a teaching statement and (if available) teaching evaluations; (6) an official transcript; and (7) three letters of recommendation. Successful candidates will have completed their Ph.D. degree in Political Science by August 1, 2027. All application materials should be submitted online to the attention of Professor Aurelian Craiutu, Department Chair, Department of Political Science at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34175 . Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, but applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Posting Details Position Details Title Open Rank Professor of Political Science – Quantitative Methods for Social Science Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Political Science Location Bloomington Position Summary Quantitative Methods for Social Science (Open Rank) The Department of Political Science at Indiana University, Bloomington invites applications for a full-time tenure track Open Rank position in the field of Quantitative Methods for Social Science, beginning August 1, 2027. Our goal is to hire the strongest candidate available who is doing interesting and important scholarship in this field and who can contribute to the Department’s mission and campus’s strengths in social sciences. Candidates should have an active research agenda with strong promise of publication in leading venues, as well as excellent teaching credentials. We seek scholars whose work has the potential to make influential contributions to the discipline and who can contribute to methods training across the empirical subfields. We are interested in candidates who advance quantitative political science, whether by applying established methods creatively and rigorously to substantive questions or by developing new approaches to data analysis. We welcome applicants working across a variety of approaches, particularly computational and Bayesian, and with a range of data, including text, survey, and panel data. In addition to maintaining an ongoing research program, the successful candidate will be expected to teach courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels and to participate actively in departmental activities. Basic Qualifications Candidates should demonstrate active research agendas with the promise for publication in high-quality venues and strong teaching credentials. In addition to maintaining an ongoing research program, this faculty member would be expected to teach courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and to participate actively in departmental activities. Department Contact for Questions Questions regarding the position or application process should be directed to Amanda Campbell, Department Manager, e-mail: accamp@iu.edu , Department of Political Science, 210 Woodburn Hall, 1100 E. Seventh Street, Indiana University-Bloomington, Bloomington, Indiana, 47405-7110. Tel: 812-855-6308. Additional Qualifications Completed Ph.D. degree in Political Science by August 1, 2027. Salary and Rank Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Special Instructions All candidates should submit: (1) a cover letter describing research completed and planned; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a research statement; (4) two writing samples; (5) a teaching portfolio with a teaching statement and (if available) teaching evaluations; (6) an official transcript; and (7) three letters of recommendation. Successful candidates will have completed their Ph.D. degree in Political Science by August 1, 2027. All application materials should be submitted online to the attention of Professor Aurelian Craiutu, Department Chair, Department of Political Science at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34175 . Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, but applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. For Best Consideration Date 10/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101652-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Evidence of Teaching Ability Statement of Teaching Philosophy Publication 1 Publication 2 Sample Syllabus Research Agenda Transcript Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34681": {
      "title": "Director of Language Instruction (DLI) in French as Lecturer of French",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Director of Language Instruction (DLI) in French as Lecturer of French Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Director of Language Instruction (DLI) in French as Lecturer of French Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should apply online at http://indiana.peopleadmin.com by providing a cover letter; CV; statement on teaching; contact information for three letters of reference; and a teaching portfolio with lesson plans, example syllabi for courses taught or created, teaching evaluations, teaching observation reports, and a video demonstrating their classroom teaching. Video should be sent in the form of a document (Word, PDF, etc.) with an embedded link to your video. Review of applications will begin November 01, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Queries can be sent to fritdept@iu.edu or steenbem@iu.edu. Posting Details Position Details Title Director of Language Instruction (DLI) in French as Lecturer of French Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington French and Italian Location Bloomington Position Summary Director of Language Instruction ( DLI ) in French as Lecturer of French Basic Qualifications The Department of French and Italian at Indiana University, Bloomington, invites applications for a Director of Language Instruction ( DLI ) in French as Lecturer in French, with the position starting on August 1, 2027. As DLI , the Lecturer will be responsible for managing all aspects of the basic French language program – including supervising graduate instructors – in collaboration with department faculty and the Director of Undergraduate Studies in French. We seek an individual who is committed to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate (and graduate) levels with native or near-native proficiency in French. Significant training or a degree specialization in language learning or instruction is required, along with a doctorate in French or a related discipline (such as, but not limited to, Second Language Acquisition or Pedagogy etc.). Candidates should have extensive teaching experience at the post-secondary level, along with evidence of pedagogical excellence as demonstrated by the teaching portfolio. Successful applicants will demonstrate the ability to design and implement curricula across multiple sections and levels, to engage in recruitment for the major, and to engage with high school French programs. The candidate will teach four courses per year in the French Language Program, including graduate pedagogy courses Department Contact for Questions Maria Sanchez Steenberger, Department Manager for the Department of French and Italian fritdept@iu.edu or steenbem@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Candidates should have extensive teaching experience at the post-secondary level, along with evidence of pedagogical excellence as demonstrated by the teaching portfolio. Successful applicants will demonstrate the ability to design and implement curricula across multiple sections and levels, to engage in recruitment for the major, and to engage with high school French programs. The candidate will teach four courses per year in the French Language Program, including graduate pedagogy courses. H1-B sponsorship is not available for this position Salary and Rank Special Instructions Applicants should apply online at http://indiana.peopleadmin.com by providing a cover letter; CV; statement on teaching; contact information for three letters of reference; and a teaching portfolio with lesson plans, example syllabi for courses taught or created, teaching evaluations, teaching observation reports, and a video demonstrating their classroom teaching. Video should be sent in the form of a document (Word, PDF , etc.) with an embedded link to your video. Review of applications will begin November 01, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Queries can be sent to fritdept@iu.edu or steenbem@iu.edu. For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101735-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Evidence of Teaching Ability Statement of Teaching Philosophy Video Sample Syllabus Course Evaluation Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
