    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34531": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Faculty Position in RNA Biology",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Faculty Position in RNA Biology Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Faculty Position in RNA Biology Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position search is being conducted concurrently with a tenured, associate professor position. To apply for the w/tenure position, visit: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34357 Posting Details Position Details Title Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Faculty Position in RNA Biology Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor in the College of Arts and Sciences , Department of Biology in the field of RNA Science and Technology . As a part of the Faculty 100 strategic initiative , we seek candidates developing innovative experimental and computational approaches to understand, visualize, or therapeutically target RNA and RNA machines, but all areas of RNA biology will be considered. Indiana University Bloomington provides a highly collaborative environment for RNA research, with existing strengths in structural biology, virology, genomics, computational biology, RNA regulation and modification, and synthetic biology. We encourage applications from scholars who apply interdisciplinary perspectives and share important research overlap with current IUB scholars, while also offering new dimensions that will expand and strengthen RNA science at IUB . Researchers have access to state-of-the-art facilities for genomics, light microscopy, physical biochemistry, structural biology (cryo-electron and crystallography) and advanced high-performance computing resources. This 10‐month appointment would ideally start August 1, 2027 , but start date is negotiable. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure-track faculty are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of the department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research program including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research as a principal investigator; teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students; and participating in service within the department, school and university and actively engaging with their professional community. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a doctoral degree and demonstrate a strong record of scholarly achievement appropriate to the level of appointment. Candidates applying at the assistant professor level should provide evidence of research productivity through first- or corresponding-author peer-reviewed publications, presentations of research at relevant scientific or professional conferences, and other indicators of scholarly impact. Candidates should also demonstrate strong potential to secure external research funding. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 2 pages in length) summarizing your qualifications, and interest in the position, including possible courses for teaching. Current Curriculum Vitae Research Statement (maximum of 3 pages in length) describing past and future work Applicants for the assistant professor position should apply at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34356 and submit the names of three references to be contacted at the time of application . All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Heather Hundley, search chairperson, at hahundle@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The position is based in the Department of Biology , a large, unified department within the College of Arts and Sciences. Biology offers strong undergraduate programs, nationally ranked graduate programs, and a broad, collaborative research environment. Research in the department spans biological questions and experimental systems across scales, from ecosystems, evolution, and organismal biology to microbiology, developmental and cell biology, molecular and systems biology, bioinformatics, and genomics. This breadth provides opportunities for interdisciplinary research and collaboration across the department and the broader IUB research community. The College of Arts and Sciences is at the academic heart of Indiana University Bloomington , the flagship campus of Indiana University. College faculty are regularly recognized with some of the nation’s and world’s highest academic and professional honors, including election to the American Academy of Arts and Sciences, the National Academies, and the American Association for the Advancement of Science, as well as MacArthur and Guggenheim Fellowships and Fulbright Awards. Located in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, Bloomington is a vibrant community of approximately 85,000 residents that combines the character of a college town with many of the cultural and recreational amenities of a larger city. The community offers theater, music, and arts events—including the LOTUS World Music & Arts Festival—as well as quick access to approximately 250,000 acres of public recreation lands and several nearby lakes. With strong public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers an attractive environment in which to live and work. Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a doctoral degree and demonstrate a strong record of scholarly achievement appropriate to the level of appointment. Candidates applying at the assistant professor level should provide evidence of research productivity through first- or corresponding-author peer-reviewed publications, presentations of research at relevant scientific or professional conferences, and other indicators of scholarly impact. Candidates should also demonstrate strong potential to secure external research funding. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Heather Hundley, search chairperson, at hahundle@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Commensurate with experience Special Instructions This position search is being conducted concurrently with a tenured, associate professor position. To apply for the w/tenure position, visit: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34357 For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101684-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Research Agenda Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34530": {
      "title": "Tenured Associate Professor Faculty Position in RNA Biology",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Tenured Associate Professor Faculty Position in RNA Biology Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Tenured Associate Professor Faculty Position in RNA Biology Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position search is being conducted concurrently with a tenure-track, assistant professor position. To apply for the tenure-track position, visit: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34356 Posting Details Position Details Title Tenured Associate Professor Faculty Position in RNA Biology Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications for a tenured associate professor in the College of Arts and Sciences, Department of Biology in the field of RNA Science and Technology . As a part of the Faculty 100 strategic initiative , we seek candidates developing innovative experimental and computational approaches to understand, visualize, or therapeutically target RNA and RNA machines, but all areas of RNA biology will be considered. Indiana University Bloomington provides a highly collaborative environment for RNA research, with existing strengths in structural biology, virology, genomics, computational biology, RNA regulation and modification, and synthetic biology. We encourage applications from scholars who apply interdisciplinary perspectives and share important research overlap with current IUB scholars, while also offering new dimensions that will expand and strengthen RNA science at IUB . Researchers have access to state-of-the-art facilities for genomics, light microscopy, physical biochemistry, structural biology (cryo-electron and crystallography) and advanced high-performance computing resources. This 10‐month appointment would ideally start August 1, 2027 , but start date is negotiable. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure-track faculty are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of the department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research program including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research as a principal investigator; teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students; and participating in service within the department, school and university and actively engaging with their professional community. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a doctoral degree and demonstrate a strong record of scholarly achievement appropriate to the level of appointment. Candidates seeking appointment at the associate professor level must demonstrate a sustained record of scholarly achievement commensurate with a tenured appointment. This should include a record of extramurally funded research as principal investigator, an established body of corresponding-author publications, evidence of visibility and engagement within the broader scholarly community, and experience leading substantial research initiatives. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 2 pages in length) summarizing your qualifications, and interest in the position, including possible courses for teaching. Current Curriculum Vitae Research Statement (maximum of 3 pages in length) describing past and future work Applicants for the associate professor position should apply at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34357 . No letters of reference are required at the time of the application but may be requested, along with additional material, as applications are reviewed. All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Heather Hundley, search chairperson, at hahundle@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by IUB with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The position is based in the Department of Biology , a large, unified department within the College of Arts and Sciences. Biology offers strong undergraduate programs, nationally ranked graduate programs, and a broad, collaborative research environment. Research in the department spans biological questions and experimental systems across scales, from ecosystems, evolution, and organismal biology to microbiology, developmental and cell biology, molecular and systems biology, bioinformatics, and genomics. This breadth provides opportunities for interdisciplinary research and collaboration across the department and the broader IUB research community. The College of Arts and Sciences is at the academic heart of Indiana University Bloomington, the flagship campus of Indiana University. College faculty are regularly recognized with some of the nation’s and world’s highest academic and professional honors, including election to the American Academy of Arts and Sciences, the National Academies, and the American Association for the Advancement of Science, as well as MacArthur and Guggenheim Fellowships and Fulbright Awards. Located in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, Bloomington is a vibrant community of approximately 85,000 residents that combines the character of a college town with many of the cultural and recreational amenities of a larger city. The community offers theater, music, and arts events—including the LOTUS World Music & Arts Festival—as well as quick access to approximately 250,000 acres of public recreation lands and several nearby lakes. With strong public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers an attractive environment in which to live and work. Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a doctoral degree and demonstrate a strong record of scholarly achievement appropriate to the level of appointment. Candidates seeking appointment at the associate professor level must demonstrate a sustained record of scholarly achievement commensurate with a tenured appointment. This should include a record of extramurally funded research as principal investigator, an established body of corresponding-author publications, evidence of visibility and engagement within the broader scholarly community, and experience leading substantial research initiatives. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Heather Hundley, search chairperson, at hahundle@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Commensurate with experience Special Instructions This position search is being conducted concurrently with a tenure-track, assistant professor position. To apply for the tenure-track position, visit: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34356 For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date Posting Number IU-101685-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Research Agenda Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34529": {
      "title": "Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Artificial Intelligence for Life Sciences",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Artificial Intelligence for Life Sciences Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Artificial Intelligence for Life Sciences Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Artificial Intelligence for Life Sciences Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications for a tenured/tenure-track faculty position in the Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering in the field of artificial intelligence for life sciences. This search seeks applicants at the assistant, associate, or full professor rank to serve as a member of the Computer Science or Intelligent Systems Engineering Department. We seek candidates who can teach and lead cutting-edge research in AI, including generative AI, to bridge biomolecular data—such as genomics and pharmaceutical mechanisms—with clinical insights into disease and targeted interventions across areas such as diabetes and cardiovascular disease. We encourage applications from scholars who apply interdisciplinary perspectives across a variety of domains and complement existing strengths within these departments in bioinformatics, artificial intelligence and machine learning, and expand cutting-edge initiatives including the recently launched B.S. in Robotics and IUB’s targeted growth in bioengineering and pre-med pathways within Intelligent Systems Engineering, directly translating theoretical AI into physical, real-world solutions. This 10‐month appointment would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by November 14, 2026, will receive full consideration, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure-track faculty at Indiana University Bloomington are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of their department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students as designated by the department chairperson; and actively providing service within the department, school and university alongside active engagement with the profession and/or the community. Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to: AI for Genomics and Systems Biology AI for Clinical Diagnosis and Personalized Medicine AI for Structural Biology and Drug Discovery Agentic AI for Life Sciences Research and Discovery Lab Automation and Bio-Instrumentation This position is located on the campus of Indiana University, Bloomington ( IUB ) in Bloomington, Indiana, and the successful candidate is expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in three areas including research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this initiative are expected to excel in research and demonstrate strong performance in teaching and service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Candidates seeking positions with tenure must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for a tenured appointment, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, an established record of publications and scholarly work, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Candidates with industry backgrounds, particularly at the intersection of AI and the life sciences, are highly encouraged to apply. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (identifying your application for a position with tenure (associate professor) or a tenure-track position (assistant professor), summarizing your qualifications, and interest in the position). Curriculum Vitae Research Statement Teaching Statement Up to three representative scholarly publications (optional) Contact information for three professional references Professional references for applicants for tenure-track positions will only be solicited for those selected for a screening interview. Professional references for applicants for positions with tenure will only be solicited for those selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Applicants should apply at: link https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34400 . All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Yuzhen Ye ( yye@iu.edu ), search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN., IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ Master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. The Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering at Indiana University is the first of its kind and among the largest in the country. Its mission is to excel and lead in education, research, and outreach spanning and integrating the full breadth of computing, information technology and modern engineering. The Luddy School is a core school with programs on the Bloomington and Indianapolis campus and includes over 150 faculty and 3000 students on the Bloomington campus. Departments on the Luddy School’s Bloomington campus include Computer Science, Information and Library Science, Informatics, and Intelligent Systems Engineering. The Luddy School and Indiana University offer an exceptional environment for research at the intersection of AI and the life sciences. Luddy has longstanding strengths in bioinformatics and AI, supported by a broad network of research centers and faculty. Opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration extend across IU, including the Luddy Artificial Intelligence Center ( LAIC ), IU School of Medicine in Bloomington and Indianapolis, and other centers spanning genomics, precision medicine, neuroscience, and biomedical data science. These academic strengths are complemented by IU LAB in Indianapolis, which connects IU researchers with a vibrant network of life-sciences companies, clinical partners, and research organizations, creating substantial opportunities for translational research, industry collaboration, and real-world impact. Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. For more information about the Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering, visit: https://luddy.indiana.edu/ Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Yuzhen Ye ( yye@iu.edu ), search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Commensurate with experience Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 11/15/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101692-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Research and Teaching Optional Documents Research Paper 1 Research Paper 2 Research Paper 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34528": {
      "title": "Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Cybersecurity",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Cybersecurity Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Cybersecurity Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Cybersecurity Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary The Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering at Indiana University Bloomington invites applications for an open rank faculty position to add to IU’s research leadership in Cybersecurity , at the assistant, associate, or full professor level. We seek exceptional researchers and educators whose work advances the theory and practice of cybersecurity to join the Department of Informatics at the Luddy School. We welcome applicants in all areas of cybersecurity but are particularly interested in candidates whose research bridges technical cybersecurity (e.g., systems/network security; applied cryptography; security informatics) and human aspects of cybersecurity (e.g., policy or governance; trusted computing; the design of usable and inclusive security and privacy technologies; security and safety of AI systems; cyber risk management; international cybersecurity policy; law and privacy; and accessible security). Successful applicants will join a collaborative academic campus-wide cybersecurity community spanning Luddy, the O’Neill School of Public Policy, Hamilton-Lugar School of Global and International Studies, Maurer School of Law, Kelley School of Business, Cognitive Science Program, Psychology and Brain Sciences, the Center for Applied Cybersecurity Research ( CACR ), and the Ostrom Workshop, with opportunities for joint appointments, cross-listed teaching, and interdisciplinary doctoral advising. The Luddy School is home to internationally recognized centers in security and privacy, and offers a supportive environment for impactful research, teaching, and mentorship. Faculty will contribute to our strong academic programs in cybersecurity, including our multi-disciplinary collaborations across campus such as the BS in Cybersecurity and Global Policy and the MS in Cybersecurity Risk Management programs. Qualified faculty may also collaborate with IU Research and the Indiana University Applied Research Center ( ARC ) in Bloomington. ARC brings together government, military, industry, and academic partners to address complex national security challenges. Within its secure facilities, researchers work on critical areas including artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, cyber-physical systems, microelectronics, autonomous systems, advanced materials, quantum computing, and other emerging technologies. These 10-month faculty appointments have a preferred start date of August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by December 1, 2026, will receive full consideration; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure track faculty at Indiana University Bloomington are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of their department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students as designated by the department chairperson; and actively providing service within the department, school, and university alongside active engagement with the profession and/or the community. These positions are located on the campus of Indiana University, Bloomington ( IUB ) in Bloomington, Indiana, and the successful candidate is expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in the three areas of research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this initiative are expected to excel in research and provide strong performance in teaching and service. Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in computer science, informatics, engineering, or a related field from an accredited educational institution, and demonstrate a strong record of research productivity and potential for (or evidence of) excellence in teaching and service. Candidates for associate and full professor positions must demonstrate a sustained record of scholarly leadership and impact appropriate for a senior career level. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin December 1, 2026 and continue until all positions are filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 3 pages in length, identifying your application for a position with tenure (associate professor/full professor) or a tenure-track position (assistant professor), summarizing your qualifications, and interest in the position. Current Curriculum Vitae Research Statement (maximum of 4 pages in length) Teaching Statement (maximum of 2 pages in length) Up to three representative scholarly publications (optional) Contact information for three professional references Professional references for applicants for tenure-track positions will only be solicited for those selected for screening interviews. Professional references for applicants for positions with tenure will only be solicited for those selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should review application requirements and apply online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34401 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Esfandiar Haghverdi, search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Indiana University provides a comprehensive benefits program for full-time appointed employees. Coverage for core benefit plans such as basic life insurance and a base retirement plan are entirely paid by the University. For detailed benefit options please visit: https://hr.iu.edu/benefits/new-employee/benefits-overview/academic-exempt.html About Indiana University Bloomington: Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, Indiana, IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB has been a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ Master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. The Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering at Indiana University is the first of its kind and among the largest in the country. Its mission is to excel and lead in education, research, and outreach spanning and integrating the full breadth of computing, information technology, and modern engineering. The Luddy School is a core school with programs on the Bloomington and Indianapolis campus and includes over 150 faculty and 3000 students. Departments in the Luddy School’s Bloomington campus include Computer Science, Information and Library Science, Informatics, and Intelligent Systems Engineering. Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off- Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. For more information about the Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering, visit: https://luddy.indiana.edu/ Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in computer science, informatics, engineering, or a related field from an accredited educational institution, and demonstrate a strong record of research productivity and potential for (or evidence of) excellence in teaching and service. Candidates for associate and full professor positions must demonstrate a sustained record of scholarly leadership and impact appropriate for a senior career level. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Esfandiar Haghverdi, search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Commensurate with experience Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 12/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101693-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Research and Teaching Optional Documents Research Paper 1 Research Paper 2 Research Paper 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34527": {
      "title": "Multiple Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Positions in Microelectronics, Circuits and Systems Design",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Multiple Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Positions in Microelectronics, Circuits and Systems Design Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Multiple Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Positions in Microelectronics, Circuits and Systems Design Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This search is running concurrently with a tenured, associate or full professor search in Microelectronics. For more information see: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34482 Posting Details Position Details Title Multiple Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Positions in Microelectronics, Circuits and Systems Design Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications for multiple tenure-track faculty positions at the assistant professor rank in the Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering, Department of Intelligent Systems Design, in the field of microelectronics, circuits, and system design. We seek candidates who can teach and lead research in one or more of the following areas: analog and mixed-signal integrated circuits; digital VLSI and AI hardware systems; advanced packaging and heterogeneous integration; and power electronics and energy-integrated microsystems . We encourage applications from scholars who apply interdisciplinary perspectives across a variety of these domains and complement existing strengths within the department. We particularly welcome candidates whose work leverages innovative computational techniques and connects microelectronic circuits and systems with computing, AI, sensing, security, radiation effects, healthcare, or other emerging application domains. These 10‐month appointments would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. All applications received prior to October 16, 2026, will receive full consideration; applications will continue to be accepted and reviewed until all positions are filled. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure-track faculty at Indiana University Bloomington are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of their department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; teaching and mentoring a diverse population of students at the undergraduate and/or graduate level as designated by the department chairperson; and actively providing service within the department, school and university alongside active engagement with the profession and/or the community. Candidates with special interest in the following areas are encouraged to apply: Analog and Mixed-Signal Integrated Circuits Key research areas: Low-power analog design; sensor interfaces; data converters ( ADC / DAC ); RF/mixed-signal integration; power management IC blocks. Teaching contributions: core electronics sequence; Analog IC Design; sensor/measurement laboratory modules; mixed-signal design projects. Digital VLSI and AI Hardware Systems Key research areas: ASIC / FPGA design flows; AI/edge accelerators; hardware–software co-design; modern SoC architectures; verification and architecture exploration. Teaching contributions: VLSI /Digital VLSI ; hardware acceleration; capstone integration; design verification and prototyping experiences. Advanced Packaging and Heterogeneous Integration Key research areas: Chiplets; 2.5D/3D integration; thermal/reliability co-design; advanced interconnects; packaging-aware design methodologies. Teaching contributions: Heterogeneous Integration & Advanced Packaging; packaging/reliability labs; cross-layer design projects linking devices to systems. Power Electronics and Energy-Integrated Microsystems Key research areas: Power ICs; wide-bandgap (GaN/SiC) integration; efficient power delivery; electrified transportation; energy-aware computing platforms. Teaching contributions: Power Electronics; power conversion labs; energy-constrained system design projects with hardware measurement. These positions are located on the campus of Indiana University, Bloomington ( IUB ) in Bloomington, Indiana, and successful candidates are expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in three areas including research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this initiative are expected to excel in research and provide strong performance in teaching and service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in engineering (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin October 16, 2026 and continue until all positions are filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 3 pages in length), identifying your application for a position with tenure (associate or full professor) or a tenure-track position (assistant professor), summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position. Current Curriculum Vitae Research Statement (maximum of 4 pages in length) Teaching Statement (maximum of 2 pages in length) Up to three representative scholarly publications (optional) Contact information for three professional references Professional references for applicants for tenure-track positions will only be solicited for those selected for screening interviews. Applicants for tenure-track, assistant professor should apply at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34481 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Daniel Loveless, search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN. IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities while fostering a culturally diverse campus environment; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ Master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. The Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering at Indiana University is the first of its kind and among the largest in the country. Its mission is to excel and lead in education, research, and outreach spanning and integrating the full breadth of computing, information technology, and modern engineering. The Luddy School is a core school with programs on the Bloomington and Indianapolis campus and includes over 150 faculty and 3000 students on the Bloomington campus. Departments on the Luddy School’s Bloomington campus include Computer Science, Information and Library Science, Informatics, and Intelligent Systems Engineering. Successful candidates will join a growing, interdisciplinary microelectronics community spanning the Luddy School and IU CREATE , with strengths in reliable and trusted electronics, radiation effects, extreme-environment and cryogenic electronics, AI hardware, photonics, security, and related areas. The new faculty will also have the opportunity to help shape IU’s expanding microelectronics research and educational programs, including the new degrees in Electrical Engineering and Microelectronics. Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. For more information about the Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering, visit: https://luddy.indiana.edu/ Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in engineering (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Daniel Loveless, search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions This search is running concurrently with a tenured, associate or full professor search in Microelectronics. For more information see: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34482 For Best Consideration Date 10/16/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101701-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Agenda Optional Documents Publication 1 Publication 2 Publication 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34526": {
      "title": "Multiple Tenured Associate or Full Professors in Microelectronics, Circuits, and Systems Design",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Multiple Tenured Associate or Full Professors in Microelectronics, Circuits, and Systems Design Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Multiple Tenured Associate or Full Professors in Microelectronics, Circuits, and Systems Design Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This search is running concurrently with a tenure-track assistant professor search in Microelectronics. For more information see: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34481 Posting Details Position Details Title Multiple Tenured Associate or Full Professors in Microelectronics, Circuits, and Systems Design Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications for multiple tenured faculty positions at the associate or full professor rank in the Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering, Department of Intelligent Systems Design, in the field of microelectronics, circuits, and system design. We seek candidates who can teach and lead research in one or more of the following areas: analog and mixed-signal integrated circuits; digital VLSI and AI hardware systems; advanced packaging and heterogeneous integration; and power electronics and energy-integrated microsystems . We encourage applications from scholars who apply interdisciplinary perspectives across a variety of these domains and complement existing strengths within the department. We particularly welcome candidates whose work leverages innovative computational techniques and connects microelectronic circuits and systems with computing, AI, sensing, security, radiation effects, healthcare, or other emerging application domains. These 10‐month appointments would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. All applications received prior to October 16, 2026, will receive full consideration; applications will continue to be accepted and reviewed until all positions are filled. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure-track faculty at Indiana University Bloomington are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of their department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; teaching and mentoring a diverse population of students at the undergraduate and/or graduate level as designated by the department chairperson; and actively providing service within the department, school and university alongside active engagement with the profession and/or the community. Candidates with special interest in the following areas are encouraged to apply: Analog and Mixed-Signal Integrated Circuits Key research areas: Low-power analog design; sensor interfaces; data converters ( ADC / DAC ); RF/mixed-signal integration; power management IC blocks. Teaching contributions: core electronics sequence; Analog IC Design; sensor/measurement laboratory modules; mixed-signal design projects. Digital VLSI and AI Hardware Systems Key research areas: ASIC / FPGA design flows; AI/edge accelerators; hardware–software co-design; modern SoC architectures; verification and architecture exploration. Teaching contributions: VLSI /Digital VLSI ; hardware acceleration; capstone integration; design verification and prototyping experiences. Advanced Packaging and Heterogeneous Integration Key research areas: Chiplets; 2.5D/3D integration; thermal/reliability co-design; advanced interconnects; packaging-aware design methodologies. Teaching contributions: Heterogeneous Integration & Advanced Packaging; packaging/reliability labs; cross-layer design projects linking devices to systems. Power Electronics and Energy-Integrated Microsystems Key research areas: Power ICs; wide-bandgap (GaN/SiC) integration; efficient power delivery; electrified transportation; energy-aware computing platforms. Teaching contributions: Power Electronics; power conversion labs; energy-constrained system design projects with hardware measurement. These positions are located on the campus of Indiana University, Bloomington ( IUB ) in Bloomington, Indiana, and successful candidates are expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in three areas including research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this initiative are expected to excel in research and provide strong performance in teaching and service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in engineering (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates for appointment with tenure positions must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for an appointment with tenure, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, established record of publications and scholarly work, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin October 16, 2026 and continue until all positions are filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 3 pages in length), identifying your application for a position with tenure (associate or full professor) or a tenure-track position (assistant professor), summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position. Current Curriculum Vitae Research Statement (maximum of 4 pages in length) Teaching Statement (maximum of 2 pages in length) Up to three representative scholarly publications (optional) Contact information for three professional references Professional references for applicants for positions with tenure will only be solicited for those selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. \\ Applicants for associate or full professor with tenure should apply at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34482 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Daniel Loveless, search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN, IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities while fostering a culturally diverse campus environment; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ Master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. The Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering at Indiana University is the first of its kind and among the largest in the country. Its mission is to excel and lead in education, research, and outreach spanning and integrating the full breadth of computing, information technology, and modern engineering. The Luddy School is a core school with programs on the Bloomington and Indianapolis campus and includes over 150 faculty and 3000 students on the Bloomington campus. Departments on the Luddy School’s Bloomington campus include Computer Science, Information and Library Science, Informatics, and Intelligent Systems Engineering. Successful candidates will join a growing, interdisciplinary microelectronics community spanning the Luddy School and IU CREATE , with strengths in reliable and trusted electronics, radiation effects, extreme-environment and cryogenic electronics, AI hardware, photonics, security, and related areas. The new faculty will also have the opportunity to help shape IU’s expanding microelectronics research and educational programs, including the new degrees in Electrical Engineering and Microelectronics. Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. For more information about the Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering, visit: https://luddy.indiana.edu/ Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in engineering (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates for appointment with tenure positions must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for an appointment with tenure, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, established record of publications and scholarly work, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Daniel Loveless, search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions This search is running concurrently with a tenure-track assistant professor search in Microelectronics. For more information see: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34481 For Best Consideration Date 10/16/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101702-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Agenda Optional Documents Publication 1 Publication 2 Publication 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
