    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34525": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Faculty Position in Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Faculty Position in Clinical Psychology Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Faculty Position in Clinical Psychology Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This search is running concurrently with an associate or full professor in clinical psychology. For more information visit: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34486 Posting Details Position Details Title Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Faculty Position in Clinical Psychology Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications at the tenure-track assistant professor rank for a cluster hire in clinical psychology in the College of Arts and Sciences, Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences. The specific area of research specialization within clinical psychology is open. Our nationally renowned Clinical Psychological Science Program brings together faculty whose research spans basic discovery through translation and population-level impact, with the broad goal of advancing the understanding of mental health problems and improving their assessment, prevention, and treatment. The IUB Clinical Psychological Science Program, which is accredited by PCSAS and APA , administers a NIMH T32 research training program in its eleventh year, and offers a first of its kind Clinical Psychological Science Bachelor of Science degree. We welcome applicants whose research and teaching will add new and/or complementary expertise and scientific perspectives to our ambitious and expanding clinical psychological science program. These 10‐month appointments would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by November 15, 2026, will receive full consideration, and applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Responsibilities: Tenure-track faculty at Indiana University Bloomington are expected to contribute substantially to the overall academic excellence of their department in research, teaching, and service, for example, by: (1) developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; (2) teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students as designated by the department chairperson; and (3) actively providing service within the department, school and university alongside active engagement with the profession and/or the community. These positions are located on the campus of Indiana University, Bloomington ( IUB ) in Bloomington, Indiana, and successful candidates are expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in three areas including research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this cluster hire are expected to excel in research and provide strong performance in teaching and service. The department provides strong support for the continued professional development of early and mid-career faculty, evidenced by a strong track record of mentoring tenure-track faculty from point of hiring to tenure and to promotion to full professor. The university provides competitive startup funds, and the department arranges service and teaching assignments so that pre-tenure faculty can prioritize time on research. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in psychology (or a related field) at the time of appointment and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for a tenure-track appointment, including, for example, experience as lead investigator of extramurally funded research, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, and established record of publications and scholarly work. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until all positions are filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 3 pages) summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position. Current curriculum vitae Research Statement (maximum of 4 pages). This statement should include a short research narrative that highlights what you find most exciting about your existing research, the key questions that excite you, and how you will develop a research program around those questions. Teaching Statement (maximum of 2 pages). This statement should include the principles that guide your teaching methods, a description of any teaching-related experiences, and what you may be interested in teaching at IUB . Up to three representative scholarly publications Contact information for three professional references. Professional references will be solicited only after an initial selection stage. Applicants should apply at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34485 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Bill Hetrick, search chairperson, at whetrick@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to (1) cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; (2) inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; (3) meaningful experiences outside the classroom; (4) expansive global educational opportunities; (5) first-rate library and museum collections; and (6) far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. The wider campus community houses many smaller communities that foster connections and belonging. Many of these groups host cultural events, workshops, and collaborative campus-wide events to build community strength. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, our campus is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful. About the College : The College of Arts and Sciences at Indiana University has over 225 academic programs rooted in three broad areas of study—Arts and Humanities, Natural and Mathematics Sciences, and Social and Historical Studies. The College is home to over 70 departments and programs and three schools—the Eskenazi School of Art, Architecture + Design, the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies, and the Media School. Over 900 faculty members serve within the College and form an extraordinary teaching and learning community at the heart of a world-class university. Members of the College’s faculty are continually recognized as elected fellows of the American Academy of Arts and Sciences, the National Academies, the American Association for the Advancement of Science, and include MacArthur and Guggenheim Fellows, Fulbright Award winners, and Pulitzer Prize, Oscar, and Emmy winners. About the Department : The Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences is home to the oldest continuing psychology laboratory in America, opened by William Lowe Bryan in 1888. Today, our core mission is to unlock the mysteries of the human brain and behavior, while preparing students to apply this knowledge globally. By translating cutting-edge discoveries to real world solutions, we train the next generation of scientists to excel in healthcare, academia, industry and public service. The department features an onsite Psychology Clinic and imaging research facility. We foster a culture where faculty are highly congenial, deeply supportive of junior faculty, and remarkably collaborative. Department policies are family friendly. To learn more about the department visit https://psych.indiana.edu . About the city : Bloomington is a vibrant university town that blends small town charm with big city cultural and athletic events. The surrounding region, featuring nature preserves, National forests, and Indiana’s largest reservoir, offers exceptional outdoor recreation opportunities. Friendly, safe, affordable and welcoming, Bloomington is a gem set in the beautiful rolling hills of southern Indiana. Bloomington’s geographic position illustrates our state’s nickname “Crossroad of America.” It is within a 1 hour drive of Indianapolis, 2 hour drive of Louisville, KY, 3.5 hour of Columbus, OH, and ~4 hour drive to Chicago, IL, St. Louis, MO, and Nashville, TN. Bloomington has a low cost of living relative to entry-level faculty salaries. The community is home to many thriving affinity groups and offers an exceptional selection of cultural, educational, and recreational opportunities. Learn more here: https://bloomington.iu.edu/campus-life/bloomington.html . Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in psychology (or a related field) at the time of appointment and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for a tenure-track appointment, including, for example, experience as lead investigator of extramurally funded research, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, and established record of publications and scholarly work. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Bill Hetrick, search chairperson, at whetrick@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions This search is running concurrently with an associate or full professor in clinical psychology. For more information visit: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34486 For Best Consideration Date 11/15/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101705-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Agenda Optional Documents Publication 1 Publication 2 Publication 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34524": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor Faculty Position in Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Associate or Full Professor Faculty Position in Clinical Psychology Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Associate or Full Professor Faculty Position in Clinical Psychology Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This search is running concurrently with an assistant professor, tenure-track position in clinical psychology. For more information visit: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34485 Posting Details Position Details Title Associate or Full Professor Faculty Position in Clinical Psychology Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications at the associate or full professor rank for a cluster hire in clinical psychology in the Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences, College of Arts and Sciences. The specific area of research specialization within clinical psychology is open. Our nationally renowned Clinical Psychological Science Program brings together faculty whose research spans basic discovery through translation and population-level impact, with the broad goal of advancing the understanding of mental health problems and improving their assessment, prevention, and treatment. The IUB Clinical Psychological Science Program is accredited by PCSAS and APA , administers a NIMH T32 research training program in its eleventh year, and offers a first of its kind Clinical Psychological Science Bachelor of Science degree. We welcome applicants whose research and teaching will add new and/or complementary expertise and scientific perspectives to our ambitious and expanding clinical psychological science program. These 10‐month appointments would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by November 15, 2026, will receive full consideration, and applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Tenure status at the time of appointment will consider the candidate’s record of accomplishment and demonstrated satisfaction of the University’s applicable standards for tenure, subject to the University’s established review and approval procedures. Responsibilities: Tenured and tenure-track faculty at Indiana University Bloomington are expected to contribute substantially to the overall academic excellence of their department in research, teaching, and service, for example, by: (1) developing and maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research both as a corresponding principal investigator and as a collaborating investigator; (2) teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students; and (3) providing service within the department, school, and university in addition to active engagement with the profession and/or the community. These positions are located on the Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) campus. Successful candidates are expected to work on campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in research, teaching, and service. All new hires are expected to excel in research and delivery high-quality teaching and service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in psychology (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for a tenured appointment, including, for example, experience as lead investigator of extramurally funded research, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, and an established record of publications and scholarly work. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until all positions are filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 3 pages) summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position. Current curriculum vitae Research Statement (maximum of 4 pages). This statement should include a short research narrative that highlights what you find most captivating about your existing research, the key questions that excite you, and how you will develop a research program around those questions. Teaching Statement (maximum of 2 pages). This statement should include the principles that guide your teaching methods, a description of any teaching-related experiences, and what you may be interested in teaching at IUB . Up to 3 representative scholarly publications Three professional references will be solicited only after an initial selection stage. Applicants should apply at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34486 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Bill Hetrick, search chairperson, at whetrick@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by IUB on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to (1) cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; (2) inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; (3) meaningful experiences outside the classroom; (4) expansive global educational opportunities; (5) first-rate library and museum collections; and (6) far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. The wider campus community houses many smaller communities that foster connections and belonging. Many of these groups host cultural events, workshops, and collaborative campus-wide events to build community strength. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, our campus is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful. About the College : The College of Arts and Sciences at Indiana University has over 225 academic programs rooted in three broad areas of study—Arts and Humanities, Natural and Mathematics Sciences, and Social and Historical Studies. The College is home to over 70 departments and programs and three schools—the Eskenazi School of Art, Architecture + Design, the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies, and the Media School. Over 900 faculty members serve within the College and form an extraordinary teaching and learning community at the heart of a world-class university. Members of the College’s faculty are continually recognized as elected fellows of the American Academy of Arts and Sciences, the National Academies, the American Association for the Advancement of Science, and include MacArthur and Guggenheim Fellows, Fulbright Award winners, and Pulitzer Prize, Oscar, and Emmy winners. About the Department : The Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences is home to the oldest continuing psychology laboratory in America, opened by William Lowe Bryan in 1888. Today, our core mission is to unlock the mysteries of the human brain and behavior, while preparing students to apply this knowledge globally. By translating cutting-edge discoveries to real world solutions, we train the next generation of scientists to excel in healthcare, academia, industry and public service. The department features an onsite Psychology Clinic and imaging research facility. We foster a culture where faculty are highly congenial, deeply supportive of junior faculty, and remarkably collaborative. Department policies are family friendly. To learn more about the department visit https://psych.indiana.edu . About the city : Bloomington is a vibrant university town that blends small town charm with big city cultural and athletic events. The surrounding region, featuring nature preserves, National forests, and Indiana’s largest reservoir, offers exceptional outdoor recreation opportunities. Friendly, safe, affordable and welcoming, Bloomington is a gem set in the beautiful rolling hills of southern Indiana. Bloomington’s geographic position illustrates our state’s nickname “Crossroad of America.” It is within a 1 hour drive of Indianapolis, 2 hour drive of Louisville, KY, 3.5 hour of Columbus, OH, and ~4 hour drive to Chicago, IL, St. Louis, MO, and Nashville, TN. Bloomington has a low cost of living relative to entry-level faculty salaries. The community is home to many thriving affinity groups and offers an exceptional selection of cultural, educational, and recreational opportunities. Learn more here: https://bloomington.iu.edu/campus-life/bloomington.html . Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in psychology (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for a tenured appointment, including, for example, experience as lead investigator of extramurally funded research, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, and an established record of publications and scholarly work. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Bill Hetrick, search chairperson, at whetrick@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions This search is running concurrently with an assistant professor, tenure-track position in clinical psychology. For more information visit: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34485 For Best Consideration Date 11/15/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101706-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Agenda Optional Documents Publication 1 Publication 2 Publication 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34508": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow, Biology Smith Lab",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Postdoctoral Fellow, Biology Smith Lab Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Postdoctoral Fellow, Biology Smith Lab Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Postdoctoral Fellow, Biology Smith Lab Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Biology Location Bloomington Position Summary The department of Biology is a large, unified department with strong undergraduate degrees, nationally-ranked graduate programs, and world-class research spanning the breadth of biological questions and experimental systems — from ecosystems to microbiology and developmental biology, from evolution to cell biology, from molecular biology to systems biology, bioinformatics, and genomics. It is always an exciting time for Biology — enormous advances in global genome analysis coupled with unprecedented developments in interdisciplinary research have made the 21st century the Century of Biology. For more information about the department, you can find it here: About: Department of Biology: Indiana University Bloomington . The Department of Biology at Indiana University Bloomington invites applications for a post-doctoral research position under the supervision of Dr. Chris Smith Home | Chris Smith . Our lab studies spatial population genetics, using simulation-based inference and machine learning to infer the evolutionary and ecological processes that shape genetic variation. The Postdoctoral Associate will conduct research exploring new inference techniques, applying cutting-edge tools to address biological questions, advancing deep learning models, or other topics discussed with the PI. We use publicly available and simulated genomic data. Core job duties include: (1) Building computational pipelines for simulation experiments and analyzing genomic sequencing data; (2), designing, implementing, and overseeing research projects focused on methods development for understanding genetic variation within and between populations; and (3) writing scientific publications and presenting findings at conferences. Other general responsibilities include: Actively participating in lab meetings and discussions. Education and experience required: Ph.D. in population genetics, computational biology, bioinformatics, computer science, or a related field. Demonstrated experience leading computational research projects is required for the proposed research. Basic Qualifications Required skills: · Experience with scientific computing · Development of reproducible analysis pipelines · Strong time management and organizational skills · Ability to work effectively as a team · Excellent written and oral communication · Dependability, initiative, and professionalism Preferred skills: · Python · Experience with population genetics. · Experience with deep learning libraries (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow) and development. Working conditions/demands: The role requires the ability to move about within an office environment. Department Contact for Questions To apply: Please submit (1) a cover letter describing your research and educational background, career goals, why you are interested in the position, and the date you are available to start; (2) a current CV; (3) the names and contact information for two references. This can be submitted at the following link: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34487 For questions about the position contact Chris Smith (chriscs@iu.edu). Timing and compensation: Applicants will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. The starting date can be adjusted to suit the candidate. The initial appointment is for one year, with potential reappointment for additional years contingent upon satisfactory performance and funding availability. Salary will be commensurate with experience and full benefits are included. Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 10/10/2026 Expected Start Date 11/01/2026 Posting Number IU-101707-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34505": {
      "title": "Tenured/Tenure-Track Assistant, Associate or Full Professor Faculty Positions in Measurement Science in Chemistry",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Tenured/Tenure-Track Assistant, Associate or Full Professor Faculty Positions in Measurement Science in Chemistry Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Tenured/Tenure-Track Assistant, Associate or Full Professor Faculty Positions in Measurement Science in Chemistry Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Tenured/Tenure-Track Assistant, Associate or Full Professor Faculty Positions in Measurement Science in Chemistry Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications for multiple, tenured/tenure-track positions at all ranks (assistant, associate or full professor) in the Department of Chemistry within the College of Arts and Sciences as a part of the Faculty 100 strategic hiring initiative. Successful candidates are expected to develop visible, externally funded research programs to address research priorities in measurement science . The department seeks scientists who develop new quantitative tools, instrumentation, and measurement approaches that answer previously inaccessible chemical, physical, and/or biological questions in any area related to chemistry. In addition to ensemble approaches, research directions may include measurements that resolve chemical and biological heterogeneity across individual molecules, particles, cells, and beyond. This initiative is intended to grow a nationally distinctive community around interdisciplinary quantitative measurement to these system -from single molecules and nanoparticles to living systems, enabled by advances in instrumentation, spectroscopy, mass spectrometry, microscopy, and machine learning. Appointments would begin August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by October 16, 2026, will receive full consideration, and applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure-track faculty at Indiana University Bloomington are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of the department by developing and maintaining a record of scholarly accomplishment, research leadership, and success or strong potential in securing competitive external research support, commensurate with rank; teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students as designated by the department chair; and actively providing service within the department, school, and university alongside active engagement with the profession and community. These positions are located on the campus of Indiana University, Bloomington ( IUB ) in Bloomington, Indiana, and successful candidates are expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in three areas: research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this initiative are expected to excel in research and demonstrate strong performance in teaching and service. Minimum Qualifications: All applicants should have a PhD in Chemistry (or a related field) and postdoctoral experience and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin October 16, 2026, and continue until all positions are filled. The following materials are required for all applicants: Cover letter In 1-2 pages, identify your application for a position with tenure (associate or full professor) or a tenure-track position (assistant professor) and summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position. Current Curriculum Vitae Research Statement In no more than 4 pages, describe your current research and future aspirations in research. Teaching Statement In no more than 2 pages, describe your teaching philosophy, experience(s) teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level, and/or your experience serving as a mentor. Contact information for three professional references Professional references for applicants for tenure-track positions will be solicited at the time of submission of application. Professional references for applicants for positions with tenure will only be solicited for those selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Application materials for all positions should be submitted at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34325 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Measurement Science Faculty Search Committee, Department of Chemistry, Indiana University, 800 E. Kirkwood Ave., Bloomington, IN 47405, chemchr@iu.edu ; or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN., IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: All applicants should have a PhD in Chemistry (or a related field) and postdoctoral experience and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Measurement Science Faculty Search Committee, Department of Chemistry, Indiana University, 800 E. Kirkwood Ave., Bloomington, IN 47405, chemchr@iu.edu ; or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Commensurate with experience Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 10/16/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101678-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Research and Teaching Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
