    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34503": {
      "title": "Tenured Associate or Full Professor in Economics",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Tenured Associate or Full Professor in Economics Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Tenured Associate or Full Professor in Economics Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position search is being conducted concurrently with an assistant professor, tenure-track position. To apply for the tenure-track rank, visit: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34453 Posting Details Position Details Title Tenured Associate or Full Professor in Economics Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Economics Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications for an tenured associate or full professor in the College of Arts and Sciences, Department of Economics . We seek candidates to join IU’s Department of Economics to lead research in areas such as Behavioral and Experimental Economics and Applied Microeconomics. Experience or interest in the use or development of artificial intelligence, machine learning, or computational tools is appreciated. These 10‐month appointments would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by October 16, 2026, will receive full consideration, and applications will be accepted and reviewed until the positions are filled. Responsibilities: Tenured faculty at Indiana University Bloomington are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of their department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio conducting cutting-edge research both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students as designated by the department chairperson; and actively providing service within the department, school and university alongside active engagement with the profession and/or the community. Candidates with special interest in the following areas are encouraged to apply: Behavioral and Experimental Economics; Applied Microeconomics These positions are located on the campus of Indiana University, Bloomington ( IUB ) in Bloomington, Indiana, and successful candidates are expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in three areas including research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this initiative are expected to excel in research and provide strong performance in teaching and service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in economics (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level.  Candidates for w/tenure positions must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for an appointment w/tenure. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin October 16, 2026and continue until the position is filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter – please summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position. Current Curriculum Vitae Research publication or job market paper Contact information for professional references: Six professional references for applicants for positions with tenure will be solicited for those selected for later stages of the selection process. Applicants for associate or full professor with tenure should apply to: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34454 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to search committee chairpersons, Prof. Daniela Puzzello or Prof. Ruli Xiao. Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN., IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ Master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. Information about the Department of Economics is available at https://economics.indiana.edu/index.html . Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in economics (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level.  Candidates for w/tenure positions must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for an appointment w/tenure. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to search committee chairpersons, Prof. Daniela Puzzello or Prof. Ruli Xiao. Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions This position search is being conducted concurrently with an assistant professor, tenure-track position. To apply for the tenure-track rank, visit: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34453 For Best Consideration Date 10/16/2026 Expected Start Date Posting Number IU-101699-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website * Identify your specific area of research expertise in the field of economics: Behavioral or Experimental Economics Applied Microeconomics Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Research Paper 1 Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34498": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Japanese Domestic Politics",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Visiting Assistant Professor of Japanese Domestic Politics Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Visiting Assistant Professor of Japanese Domestic Politics Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Visiting Assistant Professor of Japanese Domestic Politics Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington East Asian Langs & Cultures Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University-Bloomington’s Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies seeks applications for a full-time visiting assistant professor ( VAP ) of Japanese domestic politics to begin January 1, 2027. The position is for up to three consecutive teaching semesters (Spring 2027, Fall 2027, and Spring 2028), subject to campus approval. This non-tenure-track VAP position is based in Indiana University’s renowned multidisciplinary Department of East Asian Languages and Cultures ( EALC ) and partially funded by the Japan Foundation. The teaching load is two courses per semester—including one course each semester focusing specifically on some aspect of contemporary Japanese politics (broadly defined). Eligible candidates will have a PhD in political science (or related field) in hand before January 1, 2027, and combine disciplinary rigor and area studies expertise to analyze Japan and East Asian politics. Candidates whose research agenda extensively utilizes Japanese-language sources and who demonstrate an interest in contributing to Hamilton Lugar’s 21st Century Japan Politics and Society Initiative (21JPSI) will be particularly competitive. 21JPSI expects to be able to provide the successful candidate with a funded manuscript workshop and a research trip to Japan in summer 2027. This is an exciting moment to join the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies as it leads Indiana University’s international and area studies research and teaching missions. Hamilton Lugar’s EALC department boasts a robust and multidisciplinary Japan studies program, including faculty teaching on cinema, foreign affairs, history, language pedagogy, literature, music, religion, society, and visual culture. It also teaches Japanese language to over 300 students each semester. Established more than sixty years ago, the EALC department has a long history of interdisciplinarity and boasts faculty strengths in a wide array of the humanities and social sciences. The department’s mission related to research and teaching on East Asia is complemented by Hamilton Lugar’s East Asian Studies Center, the Institute of Korean Studies, and 21JPSI. Learn more at https://ealc.indiana.edu/ ; https://hls.indiana.edu/ ; and https://jpsi.indiana.edu/ . Interested applicants should send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a brief description of four possible course offerings on Japanese and/or East Asian domestic politics (broadly defined), and a list of at least two references who may be contacted about the application. Sample syllabi—especially for a Japanese domestic politics course—are welcome but not required. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled, with all applications received by August 9, 2026 being assured full consideration. Basic Qualifications PhD in political science (or related field) in hand no later than December 31, 2026 Ability to teach courses on issues related to Japanese domestic politics Department Contact for Questions For inquiries regarding the nature of the position, candidates may the Department of East Asian Languages and Cultures at ealc@iu.edu . Questions related to the submission process through the Indiana University job portal may be directed to Mr. Zac Muller, Assistant Director of Faculty Relations for the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies at zmuller@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Preference will be shown to candidates expressing interest in teaching courses with a more regional or comparative (e.g., East Asia-wide) focus and which complement existing EALC department offerings, a demonstrated track record conducting research using Japanese-language sources, and interest in contributing to the mission of 21JPSI. Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 08/09/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101534-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Proposed Course Description Optional Documents Other Sample Syllabus Other 2 Other 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34489": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant or Tenured Associate Professor Faculty Position  in Artificial Intelligence and Industrial Experiments",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Tenure-Track Assistant or Tenured Associate Professor Faculty Position  in Artificial Intelligence and Industrial Experiments Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Tenure-Track Assistant or Tenured Associate Professor Faculty Position  in Artificial Intelligence and Industrial Experiments Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Tenure-Track Assistant or Tenured Associate Professor Faculty Position  in Artificial Intelligence and Industrial Experiments Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications for one tenure-track assistant or associate professor in the Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering in the field of AI and Industrial Experiments. We seek candidates to join IU’s outstanding Computing and Engineering research program to lead research in areas such as machine learning, agentic AI, edge AI, physical AI and AI safety. We encourage applications from scholars who apply interdisciplinary perspectives and share important research overlap with current IUB scholars while also offering new dimensions that will expand and strengthen the Luddy School’s research program. These 10‐month appointments would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by November 1, 2026, will receive full consideration, and applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure-track faculty at Indiana University Bloomington are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of their department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students as designated by the department chairperson; and actively providing service within the department, school and university alongside active engagement with the profession and/or the community. We invite applications from candidates whose research advances the foundations and frontiers of artificial intelligence and its translation into industrial practice. Candidates with special interest in the following areas are encouraged to apply: machine learning methods underpinning foundation models; agentic AI and AI-based model orchestration; edge AI and resource-constrained deployment; physical and embodied AI, including industrial control, and cyber-physical systems; and trustworthy AI, covering safety, robustness, privacy, and alignment. We welcome work that spans theory, methodology, and real-world experimentation, particularly research validated through industrial-scale systems, datasets, or testbeds. Candidates with experience in industry, or with a demonstrated record of collaboration with industrial partners on applied AI problems, are especially encouraged to apply, as are those whose work bridges academic inquiry with the operational demands of deployed AI systems. These positions are located on the campus of Indiana University, Bloomington ( IUB ) in Bloomington, Indiana, and successful candidates are expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in three areas including research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this initiative are expected to excel in research and provide strong performance in teaching and service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in computer science, engineering, data science, or AI (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates considered for appointment with tenure must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate to such an appointment, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, established record of publications and scholarly work, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and continue until all positions are filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 3 pages in length, identifying your application for a position with tenure (associate professor) or a tenure-track position (assistant professor), summarizing your qualifications, and interest in the position. Current Curriculum Vitae Research Statement (maximum of 4 pages in length) Teaching Statement (maximum of 2 pages in length) OPTIONAL Up to three representative scholarly publications (optional) OPTIONAL Contact information for three professional references Professional references for applicants for tenure-track positions will only be solicited for those selected for a screening interviews. Professional references for applicants for positions with tenure will only be solicited for those selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Applicants for associate professor should apply at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34483 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Haixu Tang, search chairperson, at hatang@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN., IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ Master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. The Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering at Indiana University Bloomington is a nationally recognized leader in computing, artificial intelligence, data science, information technology, and engineering education and research. As one of the largest and most comprehensive schools of its kind in the United States, Luddy brings together distinguished faculty, innovative researchers, and talented students in a collaborative environment dedicated to advancing discovery and addressing complex societal challenges through data-driven and computational approaches. The School’s interdisciplinary Data Science Program prepares students to excel in a rapidly evolving landscape shaped by artificial intelligence and advanced analytics through rigorous training in statistics, machine learning, AI, data management, and data visualization. Supported by a vibrant research ecosystem that spans AI, intelligent systems, health informatics, cybersecurity, and computational science, the program equips graduates with the technical expertise, ethical foundation, and collaborative skills needed to transform complex data into actionable insights and innovative solutions across academia, industry, government, and the nonprofit sector. Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in computer science, engineering, data science, or AI (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates considered for appointment with tenure must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate to such an appointment, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, established record of publications and scholarly work, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Haixu Tang, search chairperson, at hatang@iu.edu or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101704-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Research Agenda Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Publication 1 Publication 2 Publication 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34467": {
