    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34436": {
      "title": "Open Rank Organizations/MHO",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Open Rank Organizations/MHO Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Open Rank Organizations/MHO Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Open Rank Organizations/MHO Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Sociology Location Bloomington Position Summary The Department of Sociology at Indiana University, Bloomington, invites applications for a rank-open (tenured or tenure-track) position beginning in the fall of 2027. We seek an individual with expertise in the sociology of organizations, interpreted broadly, who is committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. We are especially interested in candidates who use innovative methods in their research and can contribute to teaching in the undergraduate Management + Human Organization major that we administer and to substantive and methods training in our graduate program. Ph.D. is required at time of appointment. Applicants should apply online at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/hr/postings/34396 , including a cover letter; CV; statements on research and teaching; 1-3 writing samples; and three letters of reference. Review of applications will begin on October 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Queries can be sent to Art Alderson, Department Chair (aralders@iu.edu), or Andrew Halpern-Manners, Chair of the Personnel Committee (ahm@iu.edu). Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct seriously. Basic Qualifications Ph.D. in Sociology is required at time of appointment. Department Contact for Questions Art Alderson, Department Chair (aralders@iu.edu), or Andrew Halpern-Manners, Chair of the Personnel Committee (ahm@iu.edu). Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 10/16/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101694-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Writing Sample Statement of Research and Teaching List Of References Optional Documents Other Publication 1 Other 2 Other 3 Other 4 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34435": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Positions, Kelley School of Business, Business Law and Ethics",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Positions, Kelley School of Business, Business Law and Ethics Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Positions, Kelley School of Business, Business Law and Ethics Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Before a conditional oﬀer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous ﬁndings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Interested candidates should review the requirements and submit their materials at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33729 . Application materials received by September 9, 2026, will be assured of consideration. However, the search will continue until the positions are filled. · The “Statement of Teaching Philosophy” may also include a description of any relevant teaching experience and accomplishments. Applicants may also append to the Statement of Teaching Philosophy evidence of effective teaching, including peer or student teaching evaluations, instructional artifacts, and other relevant material. Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Positions, Kelley School of Business, Business Law and Ethics Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Business Law and Ethics Location Bloomington Position Summary The Business Law and Ethics department at the Kelley School of Business, Indiana University-Bloomington, seeks applications for tenured/tenure-track positions eﬀective Fall 2027. The candidate(s) selected will join a well-established department of 29 full-time faculty members who research and teach a variety of business law topics at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Departmental faculty regularly publish in top law and business journals and are known for teaching excellence. The breadth of the department’s current research and teaching interests span corporate compliance, employment, health, intellectual property, securities, sports, and technology law, white collar crime, critical thinking, and business ethics. We welcome candidates with broad research and teaching interests in business law and ethics. Specifically, we are looking to hire faculty member (s) in the general area of business law and ethics (broadly defined), and faculty member(s) specializing in corporate finance, tax, and/or mergers and acquisitions. Basic Qualifications Position(s) are anticipated to be at the assistant professor rank, though appointment at a higher rank could occur if a candidate’s record warrants. To be qualiﬁed, a candidate must have a J.D. degree with an excellent academic record (or, in the case of someone hired at the assistant rank, must demonstrate the potential to publish in top law reviews or peer-reviewed business journals), be an outstanding teacher, provide meaningful service, and contribute positively to a multicultural campus. Department Contact for Questions Candidates may direct questions to Professor Angie Raymond, Department Chair ( angraymo@iu.edu ). Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Before a conditional oﬀer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous ﬁndings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Interested candidates should review the requirements and submit their materials at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33729 . Application materials received by September 9, 2026, will be assured of consideration. However, the search will continue until the positions are filled. · The “Statement of Teaching Philosophy” may also include a description of any relevant teaching experience and accomplishments. Applicants may also append to the Statement of Teaching Philosophy evidence of effective teaching, including peer or student teaching evaluations, instructional artifacts, and other relevant material. For Best Consideration Date 09/09/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101603-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Agenda Writing Sample Optional Documents Publication 1 Publication 2 Other 2 Research Paper 2 Research Paper 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34427": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Positions, Kelley School of Business, Accounting",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Positions, Kelley School of Business, Accounting Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Positions, Kelley School of Business, Accounting Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure can be finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit an application at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33904 . Applications received before October 15, 2026 will be assured full consideration; however, applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Positions, Kelley School of Business, Accounting Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Accounting Location Bloomington Position Summary The Accounting Department at the Kelley School of Business, Indiana University-Bloomington invites applications for open rank tenure-track faculty positions to begin fall 2027. These positions are based at the IUB campus in Bloomington, Indiana. Faculty members are expected to work on campus to fully engage with the department, school, campus, and community. Basic Qualifications Candidates at the entry level must have completed all requirements for a Ph.D. degree or have completed all but dissertation in accounting or a related field at the time of appointment and have a strong commitment to excellence in scholarly research and teaching. Candidates at the advanced assistant, associate, or full professor level must have a Ph.D. in accounting or a related field and have a record of high-quality publications and demonstrated teaching excellence. Department Contact for Questions Candidates should direct any questions to Ken Merkley, Chair of the Department of Accounting ( kenmerk@iu.edu ). Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure can be finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit an application at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33904 . Applications received before October 15, 2026 will be assured full consideration; however, applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. For Best Consideration Date 10/15/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101617-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Research Paper 1 Research Paper 2 Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Ability Research Paper 3 Statement of Research and Teaching Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
