    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34426": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate or Full Professor, Department of Criminology and Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant or Associate or Full Professor, Department of Criminology and Criminal Justice Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant or Associate or Full Professor, Department of Criminology and Criminal Justice Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant or Associate or Full Professor, Department of Criminology and Criminal Justice Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Criminology and Criminal Justice Location Bloomington Position Summary The Department of Criminology and Criminal Justice at Indiana University, Bloomington invites applications for one open rank position, tenure-track or tenured, beginning the fall of 2027. We seek an individual with expertise in criminology and/or criminal justice with a specialization in victimology. Candidates must have a PhD in hand by the start date of the appointment; current ABDs are welcome to apply. Applicants’ degree must be in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or a closely related social science discipline. Applicants with only a law degree (JD, LLM , SJD ) will not be considered. We seek an individual committed to excellence in both scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Applicants should demonstrate the ability to maintain an active research agenda, mentor and supervise students, and provide service to the Department, University, and academic community. The Department of Criminology and Criminal Justice, housed in the College of Arts & Sciences, has a long and distinguished record of nationally recognized scholarship, teaching, and service, offering degrees at the bachelors, masters, and PhD levels. Its graduate program currently has 24 research active PhD students, and its undergraduate program routinely has around 700 majors. The department is one of the oldest in the country with an established interdisciplinary history. Faculty members are involved in a wide array of research, funded by major public agencies and private foundations, while also working closely with leading state and local criminal justice agencies. For more information about the Department, please visit the department’s website at https://criminaljustice.indiana.edu/ . Indiana University has nearly 90,000 students enrolled in more than 980 academic programs across nine campuses. IU Bloomington, the flagship campus, offers over 500 undergraduate and graduate degree programs. Founded in 1820, the university is designated as a Carnegie R1 institution, providing extensive support for both internal and external grants, teaching, and international collaborations. Applicants should apply online at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34406 including (1) a cover letter outlining the applicant’s qualifications, and research and teaching goals; (2) a complete curriculum vitae; and (3) contact information for three letters of reference. Review of applications will begin October 23rd, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position or application process can be directed to Dr. Adam Ghazi-Tehrani, Search Committee Chair, Department of Criminology and Criminal Justice, 1033 E. 3rd St., 346 Sycamore Hall, Bloomington, IN 47405-7005 or aghazite@iu.edu . Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct seriously. Basic Qualifications We seek an individual with expertise in criminology and/or criminal justice with a specialization in victimology. Candidates must have a PhD in hand by the start date of the appointment; current ABDs are welcome to apply. Applicants’ degree must be in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or a closely related social science discipline. Applicants with only a law degree (JD, LLM , SJD ) will not be considered. Department Contact for Questions Questions regarding the position or application process can be directed to Dr. Adam Ghazi-Tehrani, Search Committee Chair, Department of Criminology and Criminal Justice, 1033 E. 3rd St., 346 Sycamore Hall, Bloomington, IN 47405-7005 or aghazite@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 10/23/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101697-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34417": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Music (Percussion); Tenured or Tenure-track position",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Music (Percussion); Tenured or Tenure-track position Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Music (Percussion); Tenured or Tenure-track position Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. A complete application consists of a letter of application, curriculum vitae, and information about three professional references. You will be asked to provide the name, title, e-mail address, and other information for each of your reference providers. For candidates who advance in this search, an email message with instructions about uploading letters of reference will be sent automatically to each of your provided references. Candidates who advance in this search may be asked to provide additional audio and/or visual materials. Please do not send audio/video files or other materials until requested to do so. If you need help completing your application, contact Rachel Patrick, (812) 855-5541, rnpatric@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Deadline: Applications received by September 26, 2026 will be assured full consideration, however the search will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Music (Percussion); Tenured or Tenure-track position Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Percussion Location Bloomington Position Summary The Jacobs School of Music seeks candidates for a position in the Percussion Department in general/orchestral percussion/timpani. Applicants who also possess skills in the areas of drum set and/or world percussion are encouraged to apply. Regardless of the areas of specialization, expertise and versatility in teaching all aspects of percussion will be expected. The successful candidate will be able to attract highly talented students and will be able to prepare them for careers as percussionists in a wide variety of settings. Studio instruction for undergraduate and graduate percussion students as well as chamber music coaching. Orchestral repertoire class (percussion/timpani) may also be a component of this job. Participation in school‐wide committees and departmental hearings, auditions, recruitment, master classes, and other activities is expected. Basic Qualifications Established national/international reputation and demonstrated ability as a performer and teacher, able to attract highly talented students. Significant experience in general/orchestral percussion/timpani performance. Master’s degree required, doctorate preferred; comparable professional experience will be given equal consideration. Department Contact for Questions Questions: Rachel Patrick, Office of the Executive Associate Dean: (812) 855-5541; rnpatric@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Salary and rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Special Instructions A complete application consists of a letter of application, curriculum vitae, and information about three professional references. You will be asked to provide the name, title, e-mail address, and other information for each of your reference providers. For candidates who advance in this search, an email message with instructions about uploading letters of reference will be sent automatically to each of your provided references. Candidates who advance in this search may be asked to provide additional audio and/or visual materials. Please do not send audio/video files or other materials until requested to do so. If you need help completing your application, contact Rachel Patrick, (812) 855-5541, rnpatric@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Deadline: Applications received by September 26, 2026 will be assured full consideration, however the search will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. For Best Consideration Date 09/26/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101646-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34409": {
      "title": "Tenured/Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor Faculty Position in Quantum Computer Science",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Tenured/Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor Faculty Position in Quantum Computer Science Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Tenured/Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor Faculty Position in Quantum Computer Science Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Tenured/Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor Faculty Position in Quantum Computer Science Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) invites applications for a tenured/tenure-track assistant or associate professor in the Department of Computer Science, Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering in the field of quantum computer science. As a part of the Faculty 100 strategic hiring initiative, IUB seeks scholars who can help shape the theoretical foundations of quantum computing, software systems, security frameworks, and applications of emerging quantum technologies. [UI1] We encourage applications from scholars who apply interdisciplinary perspectives and share important research that overlaps with current IUB scholars while also offering new dimensions that will expand and strengthen the IUB’s quantum computing research program. These 10‐month appointments would ideally start August 1, 2027, although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by November 1, 2026, will receive full consideration, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure-track faculty at IUB are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of their department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students as designated by the department chairperson; and actively providing service within the department, school and university alongside active engagement with the profession and/or the community. Candidates with special interest in the following areas are encouraged to apply: Quantum security, cryptography, and post-quantum cryptography Quantum error correction and fault-tolerant quantum computing Quantum algorithms and complexity theory Quantum optimization and quantum machine learning Quantum programming languages, compilers, architectures, and verification These positions are located on the campus of IUB in Bloomington, Indiana, and successful candidates are expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in three areas: research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this initiative are expected to excel in research and provide strong performance in teaching and service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in computer science (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates for a position with tenure must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for an appointment with tenure, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, established record of publications and scholarly work, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and continue until all positions are filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 3 pages in length, identifying your application for a position with tenure (associate professor) or a tenure-track position (assistant professor), summarizing your qualifications, and interest in the position. Current Curriculum Vitae Research Statement (maximum of 4 pages in length) Teaching Statement (maximum of 2 pages in length) Up to three representative scholarly publications (optional) Contact information for three professional references Professional references for applicants for tenure-track positions will only be solicited for those selected for screening interviews. Professional references for applicants for positions with tenure will only be solicited for those selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Applicants for associate or full professor should apply at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34402 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Amr Sabry, search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, OVPFAA F100 search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. About Indiana University Bloomington: Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN., IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ Master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. The Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering at Indiana University is the first of its kind and among the largest in the country. Its mission is to excel and lead in education, research, and outreach spanning and integrating the full breadth of computing, information technology and modern engineering. The Luddy School is a core school with programs on the Bloomington and Indianapolis campus and includes over 150 faculty and 3000 students on the Bloomington campus. Departments on the Luddy School’s Bloomington campus include Computer Science, Information and Library Science, Informatics, and Intelligent Systems Engineering. Successful candidates will join the vibrant, multidisciplinary quantum community at IUB and have opportunities to interact and collaborate with colleagues across campus-wide quantum initiatives, including the Quantum Research Network and IU-QSEc . Additionally, IUB is a member of the multi-institutional Center for Quantum Technologies and the Midwest Quantum Collaboratory. Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. For more information about the Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering, visit: https://luddy.iu.edu/ Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in computer science (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Amr Sabry, search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, OVPFAA F100 search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Commensurate with experience Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101695-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact:  At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact:  Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact:  Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement:  Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement:  IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement:  Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Research and Teaching Optional Documents Research Paper 1 Research Paper 2 Research Paper 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34398": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Postdoctoral Fellow Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Postdoctoral Fellow Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications received by October 21, 2026 will receive full consideration. However, we will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and apply online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34381 We will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Application Materials: 1) CV 2) Contact information for 2-3 references Posting Details Position Details Title Postdoctoral Fellow Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Intelligent Systems Engineering Location Bloomington Position Summary The Jiang Lab invites applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher position. The postdoctoral researcher will lead independent research projects focused on developing next-generation neurotechnology and biomedical imaging methods, with particular emphasis on optical, ultrasound, and photoacoustic technologies. Working under the supervision of Dr. Ying Jiang, the candidate will contribute to the development of innovative approaches for neural circuit interrogation while collaborating with interdisciplinary research teams and mentoring graduate and undergraduate students. This is an excellent opportunity for early-career scientists looking to develop a strong publication record and build an independent research trajectory within a highly collaborative and well-resourced environment. Responsibilities include designing and conducting experiments, developing and integrating photoacoustic and ultrasound systems, validating technologies in animal models, and performing quantitative data analysis and computational modeling. The researcher will be expected to prepare manuscripts and conference presentations, contribute to grant proposals, help establish new technical capabilities and research directions within the laboratory, and work independently while contributing to a dynamic and collaborative research environment. Basic Qualifications Required: Ph.D. in biomedical engineering, electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, applied physics, neuroscience, or a closely related field Strong record of peer-reviewed publications Substantial hands-on experience in experimental system development, instrumentation, or quantitative biomedical research Strong programming and data-analysis skills in MATLAB and/or Python Demonstrated ability to independently design experiments, troubleshoot complex technical problems, analyze data, and communicate research findings Excellent written and oral communication skills Department Contact for Questions Questions may be sent to: Dr. Ying Jiang ( jiang16@iu.edu ) Additional Qualifications Preferred Skills: Research experience in optics, ultrasound/acoustics, photoacoustics, biomedical imaging, neuromodulation, or neuroengineering, particularly experience involving the development, integration, calibration, or characterization of optical or ultrasound instrumentation. Salary and Rank Special Instructions Applications received by October 21, 2026 will receive full consideration. However, we will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and apply online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34381 We will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Application Materials: 1) CV 2) Contact information for 2-3 references For Best Consideration Date 10/21/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101690-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34397": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Research Associate Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Research Associate Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications received by October 21, 2026 will receive full consideration. However, we will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and apply online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34391 We will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Application Materials: 1) CV 2) Brief Statement of Research 3) Contact information for at least 2 references Posting Details Position Details Title Research Associate Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Intelligent Systems Engineering Location Bloomington Position Summary The Jiang Lab invites applications for a Research Associate position. The Research Associate will contribute to research focused on developing next-generation technologies for neurotechnology, biomedical imaging, and neural circuit interrogation under the supervision of Dr. Ying Jiang. The successful candidate will support the development and implementation of advanced ultrasound and photoacoustic systems for biomedical applications while working collaboratively within a dynamic and interdisciplinary research environment. This is an excellent opportunity for individuals seeking to expand their technical expertise in biomedical imaging and neurotechnology while contributing to innovative research with translational impact. Responsibilities may include experimental setup and testing, data acquisition and analysis, programming, instrumentation development, and support of research projects involving cells and other biological systems. The Research Associate will assist with the development and optimization of imaging systems, contribute to research studies, maintain laboratory operations, and support ongoing scientific initiatives within the laboratory. Interested applicants should submit a CV/resume and a brief statement describing their research interests, relevant technical experience, and career goals. Basic Qualifications Required Education: Bachelor’s degree in biomedical engineering, electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, physics, neuroscience, or a related field. Required Experience: At least 1 year of prior hands-on engineering or research experience involving optics, ultrasound/acoustics, imaging systems, or related instrumentation is preferred. Strong problem-solving, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in an interdisciplinary research environment. Department Contact for Questions Questions may be sent to: Dr. Ying Jiang ( jiang16@iu.edu ) Additional Qualifications Preferred Qualifications: Experience with scientific programming in MATLAB or Python is highly encouraged. Salary and Rank Special Instructions Applications received by October 21, 2026 will receive full consideration. However, we will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and apply online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34391 We will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Application Materials: 1) CV 2) Brief Statement of Research 3) Contact information for at least 2 references For Best Consideration Date 10/21/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101689-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Statement of Research and Teaching List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
