      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Open Rank Non-Tenure Track Positions, Kelley School of Business (Finance) Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Open Rank Non-Tenure Track Positions, Kelley School of Business (Finance) Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The required document listed as “Other” should provide a brief description of the applicant’s relevant industry experience as it relates to the position advertised. Interested individuals should review position requirements and apply at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34072. Applications received before October 10, 2026, will be given full consideration; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Details Title Open Rank Non-Tenure Track Positions, Kelley School of Business (Finance) Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Finance Location Bloomington Position Summary The Finance Department of the Kelley School of Business, Indiana University is seeking individuals to fill an open rank non-tenure track faculty position beginning fall 2027. The classification of this position is open depending on experience and will be at the Clinical or Lecturer classification. Teaching duties of 18 credit hours a year will be primarily at the undergraduate level but may include graduate level courses. Candidates should also be open to the service commitment required of clinical faculty. Service commitments may include leading one of the Kelley School’s undergraduate workshops or MBA -level academies and serving on various department/school committees. We are seeking individuals who will be successful in working with various faculty and student groups and can manage relationships with our corporate partners. We expect that the successful candidate will grow into a leadership role in our teaching programs. Basic Qualifications Appointments at the clinical classification require a PhD, or doctoral degree completion by August 2027, in finance or related areas and finance industry experience. Appointments at the lecturer classification require a minimum of a master’s degree in finance or related fields at the time of hiring. Candidates with at least one year of relevant industry experience, specifically those who have worked in high impact roles in Financial Services and/or Corporate Finance are encouraged to apply. Those who have taught courses in Fintech and Investments or whose experience lies in these areas are particularly encouraged to apply. Department Contact for Questions Those desiring further information on these positions may contact: Chair of the Finance Department, KSBFIN@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions The required document listed as “Other” should provide a brief description of the applicant’s relevant industry experience as it relates to the position advertised. Interested individuals should review position requirements and apply at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34072. Applications received before October 10, 2026, will be given full consideration; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. For Best Consideration Date 10/10/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101636-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Other Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Ability Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
