area to begin fall 2027. Basic Qualifications For a candidate to be considered at the Clinical classification, a Ph.D. or DBA degree in management or a related field is required and must be completed by no later than August 2027. Candidates to be considered at the Lecturer classification must have a master’s degree in the area of appointment (management, organizational behavior, human resource management, or related field. We encourage applications from candidates with significant professional experience and, ideally, experience teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels; teaching experience in the online modality is also highly desirable. Department Contact for Questions Questions regarding the positions or application process can be directed to Ms. Jennifer Wyrick (mgmtrecr@iu.edu ). Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit their application at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33679 . Applications must be received by October 5, 2026 to be assured of full consideration; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. For Best Consideration Date 10/05/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101597-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Evidence of Teaching Ability Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Sample Syllabus Course Evaluation Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
