    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34759": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow in Quantum Materials and Quantum Optics",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Postdoctoral Fellow in Quantum Materials and Quantum Optics Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Postdoctoral Fellow in Quantum Materials and Quantum Optics Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications received by October 5, 2026 will receive full consideration. However, we will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and apply online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34134 We will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Application Materials: 1) CV 2) Cover Letter 3) Contact information for at least 3 references Posting Details Position Details Title Postdoctoral Fellow in Quantum Materials and Quantum Optics Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Intelligent Systems Engineering Location Bloomington Position Summary Working under the direction of Dr. Iqbal Utama, the postdoctoral fellow will lead experimental research focused on low-dimensional, molecular, and hybrid organic–inorganic materials for applications in quantum sensing, quantum photonics, and related quantum technologies. The successful candidate will design, fabricate, and characterize quantum materials and nanoscale devices, contribute to scientific publications and research proposals, and mentor graduate and undergraduate students in a collaborative research environment. This is an outstanding opportunity for early-career researchers to advance an independent research program, build a strong publication record, and contribute to cutting-edge developments in quantum science and technology within a highly interdisciplinary and well-supported academic setting. Specific Duties: Conduct experimental research on low-dimensional, molecular, and hybrid organic–inorganic materials for quantum sensing, quantum photonics, and related quantum technologies. Design, fabricate, and characterize quantum-material and nanoscale devices using techniques that may include materials synthesis and processing, nanofabrication, optical spectroscopy, scanning probe microscopy, magnetometry, and optically-detected magnetic resonance. Develop experimental protocols and assist with the setup, operation, maintenance, and documentation of laboratory instruments. Analyze and interpret experimental data and maintain complete, organized records of experiments, procedures, and results. Prepare manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed journals and present research findings at scientific meetings. Contribute to the preparation of research proposals, technical reports, and collaborative projects. Mentor graduate and undergraduate students and provide training in relevant laboratory methods. Contribute to a safe, collegial, collaborative, and intellectually engaged laboratory environment. Anticipated start date: December 1, 2026, or a mutually agreed date thereafter. Anticipated end date: November 30, 2027, based on a December 1, 2026 start date. Appointment term: The initial appointment will be for 12 months. The appointment may be renewed annually, subject to satisfactory performance and availability of funding. Basic Qualifications Required Education: Ph.D. completed by the appointment start date. This degree must be in Physics; Chemistry; Materials Science and Engineering; Electrical Engineering; Chemical Engineering; Applied Physics; or a closely related field. Required Experience: Relevant hands-on experimental research experience obtained during the candidate’s doctoral training is required and is described in the position qualifications. Department Contact for Questions Questions may be sent to: Dr. Iqbal Utama ( iqutama@iu.edu ) Additional Qualifications Preferred Qualifications: Experience in one or more of the following areas is preferred: Two-dimensional or other low-dimensional materials. Molecular, organic, or hybrid organic–inorganic materials. Cleanroom nanofabrication, including electron-beam or optical lithography, thin-film deposition, etching, or atomic layer deposition. Optical spectroscopy, confocal microscopy, time-resolved spectroscopy, or single-photon measurements. Optically detected magnetic resonance, spin resonance, quantum sensing, or scanning-probe magnetometry. Scanning probe microscopy and related techniques. Construction, modification, automation, or troubleshooting of optical measurement systems. Simulation of light–matter interactions using software packages such as Lumerical FDTD and COMSOL Multiphysics Salary and Rank Special Instructions Applications received by October 5, 2026 will receive full consideration. However, we will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and apply online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34134 We will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Application Materials: 1) CV 2) Cover Letter 3) Contact information for at least 3 references For Best Consideration Date 10/05/2026 Expected Start Date 12/01/2026 Posting Number IU-101649-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34758": {
      "title": "Center for Possible Minds Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Center for Possible Minds Postdoctoral Fellow Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Center for Possible Minds Postdoctoral Fellow Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Center for Possible Minds Postdoctoral Fellow Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Arts & Sciences; Dean Location Bloomington Position Summary Center for Possible Minds Postdoctoral Fellow Vacancy The Center for Possible Minds at Indiana University, Bloomington, invites applications for Postdoctoral Fellows to join its Program for Advanced Research in Diverse Intelligences. The fellowship provides support to scholars studying intelligence/cognition/mind in diverse forms, from diverse disciplinary perspectives. Candidates must embrace interdisciplinary scholarship and be excited about substantial conversation and collaboration with other disciplines. This postdoctoral fellowship program aims to create a cohort of researchers optimally positioned to address questions about the nature of biological, artificial, and collective intelligence through collaboration across a wide range of fields. We seek enthusiastic scientists and scholars who will embrace the chance to help set the agenda for our new research center. Postdoctoral fellows will have the opportunity to organize meetings and workshops at the Center as well as to propose new Center initiatives. We expect to hire 2-4 postdocs through this search. Postdocs will have offices in the Center for Possible Minds, where they will be joined by visiting fellows and faculty. Fellows are expected to pursue research activities associated with their primary area(s) of scholarship, as well as to explore collaborative, interdisciplinary projects. These fellowships are designed to advance the careers of new scholars by providing opportunities to research, organize, and collaborate in a highly interdisciplinary environment. Strong applicants will demonstrate evidence of the sort of outstanding scholarly potential that would make them competitive for tenure-track faculty positions at Indiana University or other top research universities. Terms of Agreement Fellows are expected to pursue research, organize workshops and events, and participate in Center activities and seminars. Fellows may also teach classes in the appropriate department(s) or program(s), subject to curriculum needs and availability of funds. Fellowships are expected to be 2-year positions; fellows will be appointed as one-year contracts with the possibility for renewal. The start date is flexible; positions can begin as soon as August 1, 2026. Fellows will receive a salary of $60,000 plus health benefits and $3,000 each year in research support. Application Process We invite applications from qualified candidates at the beginning of their academic careers who do not yet hold tenure-track academic positions. Applicants should submit the following materials: (1) a cover letter; (2) their CV; (3) a research statement describing their research and professional goals; (4) a one-page statement describing activities and initiatives they hope to organize through the Center; and (5) the names of 3 referees. Applications should be submitted online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/32986 . Cover letters should be addressed to: Professors Erica Cartmill and Jacob Foster, Center for Possible Minds, Indiana University, 815 10th St., Bloomington, IN 47405. Please send any questions to ericac@iu.edu and jacobf@iu.edu . Applications received by May 10, 2026 at 12:00 pm EST will receive full consideration. Basic Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D. in hand by the time they start the fellowship. Department Contact Applications should be submitted online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/32986 . Cover letters should be addressed to: Professors Erica Cartmill and Jacob Foster, Center for Possible Minds, Indiana University, 815 10th St., Bloomington, IN 47405. Queries should be sent to ericac@iu.edu and jacobf@iu.edu . Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Basic Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D. in hand by the time they start the fellowship. Department Contact for Questions Applications should be submitted online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/32986 . Cover letters should be addressed to: Professors Erica Cartmill and Jacob Foster, Center for Possible Minds, Indiana University, 815 10th St., Bloomington, IN 47405. Queries should be sent to ericac@iu.edu and jacobf@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 05/10/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2026 Posting Number IU-101554-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Research Agenda Statement of Research and Teaching List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34735": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Exercise Science Department of Kinesiology",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Lecturer of Exercise Science Department of Kinesiology Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Lecturer of Exercise Science Department of Kinesiology Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Procedure: Please provide a) curriculum vitae, b) cover letter (2 pages maximum), c) teaching statement (3 pages maximum), and d) a minimum of three (3) references. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34516 . Posting Details Position Details Title Lecturer of Exercise Science Department of Kinesiology Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Kinesiology Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) School of Public Health‐Bloomington (SPH‐B) invites applications for the position of Lecturer of Exercise Science in the Department of Kinesiology. The SPH -B seeks passionate, contemporary educators who will contribute to excellence in teaching and student learning in the study and application of human movement, physical activity, exercise, and human performance, preparing students for continued education and professional careers in kinesiology, allied health, or related fields. This 10-month instructional faculty appointment is planned to start August 1, 2027 . Appointment may be made at the rank of Lecturer, Senior Lecturer, or Teaching Professor, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applications received by November 15, 2026, will receive full priority consideration, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. This position is located on the Bloomington campus of Indiana University. Successful candidates are expected to work on campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, university, and community. Responsibilities and Opportunity: Non-tenure-track faculty or instructional faculty, Lecturers, are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of the department primarily through teaching and student learning; developing, delivering, and enhancing courses and curricula within their areas of expertise; mentoring and supporting undergraduate and/or graduate students as appropriate to their assigned responsibilities; and engaging in ongoing professional development and other activities that support excellence in teaching, student learning, curriculum enhancement, and student success. The position may provide opportunities to contribute to the department through service in support of teaching and academic program delivery, such as internship coordination, experiential or service-learning initiatives, and community outreach. Notably, instructional faculty, including Lecturers, have an opportunity for promotion and advancement from Lecturer to Senior Lecturer and ultimately to the highest rank of Teaching Professor. The ideal candidate will contribute to the teaching mission of the department in exercise science, with the ability to support related areas of the curriculum including physical activity, health promotion, and pre-professional health preparation. About Kinesiology : As a legacy program on the IUB campus, the Department of Kinesiology, with 30 full-time faculty, has a strong and growing enrollment in the undergraduate Exercise Science degree program (~1,375 students), and healthy enrollments in graduate degree programs (~75 students) including an MS in Athletic Training, MS in Kinesiology, and a PhD in Human Performance. Faculty conduct research across numerous areas including exercise physiology (with historical excellence in environmental and clinical exercise physiology), biomechanics, sport neurotrauma, athletic training neuromuscular/motor control, physical activity and fitness interventions, with the latter including youth sport-based approaches to health and well-being. Finally, the department supports the Physical Activity Instruction Program, an extensive fitness and sport focused academic service program. About SPH -B : The SPH -B is in the heart of the Bloomington campus and comprises five collaborative academic departments with 300 faculty and staff. With approximately 4,600 students, including approximately 470 graduate students, and 160 faculty members, SPH -B is well positioned to meet the challenges and opportunities of contemporary higher education. In addition to the SPH -B Office of Online Education, IUB also provides SPH -B faculty outstanding teaching support through programs like the Faculty Academy on Excellence in Teaching (F.A.C.E.T.); extensive research development and research administrative support through the Office of the Vice President for Research; and innovative collaborations with organizations such as the Indianapolis Colts, Indiana University Athletics, the U.S. National Park Service, and a wealth of local, national, and international partners to broaden the scope of the faculty and student experience. SPH -B continues its rapid expansion, embracing a comprehensive and holistic approach to promoting health and wellbeing within the research, teaching, and service aspects of our mission. With an emphasis on high-quality, impactful research, excellence in teaching and mentoring, and meaningful and impactful service, there has never been a more exciting time to join our growing and evolving team. About IUB : Founded in 1820, Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University and is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. A member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, IUB prides itself in offering outstanding academics grounded in world class research and a vibrant campus life with 48,000+ students and 16 degree-granting schools and colleges. IUB offers 200+ undergraduate majors as well as extensive graduate and professional study opportunities, including 90+ master’s degrees and 80+ Ph.D. programs. IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is also considered by many to be one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. About Bloomington : Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all Basic Qualifications Qualifications: A successful candidate will have a Ph.D. or master’s degree in exercise science or a closely related field (e.g., public health, physical therapy, etc.) that aligns with the department’s teaching needs. Preference will be given to candidates with teaching and/or professional experience in the field. Candidates must demonstrate effective teaching skills and the ability to contribute to high-quality instruction and student learning in their area of expertise. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work effectively and collegially with faculty, staff, and students are required. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to contribute to curriculum development, instructional innovation, student mentoring, and other activities that support the teaching mission of the department and school, as appropriate to their assigned responsibilities. Candidates for appointments at the Senior Lecturer or Teaching Professor rank must demonstrate teaching experience and accomplishments appropriate to the proposed rank. Appointment at the Senior Lecturer or Teaching Professor rank will require evidence of accomplishments and experience consistent with Indiana University criteria for the proposed rank. Department Contact for Questions Questions: · Questions about the PeopleAdmin application procedure may be directed to Dave Archer at dwarcher@iu.edu . · Questions regarding the position may be directed to Lisa Koontz, Director of Faculty Operations, lmkoontz@iu.edu , or Grace Sembajwe, Executive Associate Dean, gsembajw@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Application Procedure: Please provide a) curriculum vitae, b) cover letter (2 pages maximum), c) teaching statement (3 pages maximum), and d) a minimum of three (3) references. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34516 . For Best Consideration Date 11/15/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101709-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 2 Other 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34734": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Parks, Recreation and the Outdoors / Generalist",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Lecturer of Parks, Recreation and the Outdoors / Generalist Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Lecturer of Parks, Recreation and the Outdoors / Generalist Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Procedure: Please provide (1) a curriculum vitae and (2) a cover letter no longer than five pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, including a statement of your teaching interests, experience, and approach to supporting student learning. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34585 Posting Details Position Details Title Lecturer of Parks, Recreation and the Outdoors / Generalist Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington School of Public Health Location Bloomington Position Summary The Indiana University School of Public Health‐Bloomington (SPH‐B) invites applications for the position of Lecturer of Parks, Recreation, and the Outdoors, who will also contribute as a generalist in the Department of Sport Management, Tourism, & Recreation ( SMTR ). This 10-month appointment would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by December 14, 2026 , will receive full priority consideration, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Responsibilities: As non-tenure-track faculty, Lecturers are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of the department through excellence in teaching and student learning; the development, delivery, and enhancement of courses and curricula within their areas of expertise; the mentoring and supporting undergraduate and/or graduate students as appropriate; and professional development and scholarly or creative activities that support teaching and student learning. This role is comprised of primarily teaching in the area of parks and recreation. The successful candidate will also be expected to contribute as a generalist to broader departmental needs. About IUB : Founded in 1820, Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University and has been a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909. Indiana University Bloomington prides itself in offering outstanding academics grounded in world class research and vibrant campus life. Located in Bloomington, IN, IUB strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. Indiana University Bloomington is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. The campus enrolls more than 48,000 students and is home to 16 degree-granting schools and colleges. IU Bloomington offers more than 200 undergraduate majors as well as extensive graduate and professional study opportunities, including more than 90 master’s degrees and more than 80 Ph.D. programs. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IU Bloomington is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. For more information about Indiana University Bloomington, visit https://bloomington.iu.edu/ . About SPH -B: The School of Public Health-Bloomington ( SPH -B) is located in the heart of the Bloomington campus and comprises five collaborative academic departments with 300 faculty and staff. Indiana University provides IU SPH -B faculty outstanding teaching and research support through programs like the Faculty Academy on Excellence in Teaching (F.A.C.E.T.); extensive research development and research administrative support through the Office of the Vice President for Research; and innovative collaborations with organizations such as the NCAA , the Indianapolis Colts, Indiana University Athletic Department, the US National Park Service, and a wealth of local, national, and international partners to broaden the scope of the faculty and student experience. SPH -B continues its rapid expansion embracing a comprehensive and holistic approach to promoting health and wellbeing within the research, teaching, and service aspects of our mission. With an emphasis on high-quality, impactful research, excellence in teaching, and meaningful service, there has never been a more exciting time to join our growing and evolving team. For more information about the School of Public Health – Bloomington, visit https://www.publichealth.indiana.edu/ . About Bloomington: Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. For more information about Bloomington, IN, visit https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34585 . Basic Qualifications Qualifications: Candidates must hold a master’s degree or higher, with a preference given to those holding a doctoral degree, in Recreation/Leisure or a closely related field from a reputable, well-established institution. Candidates must have professional experience in the field of parks, recreation, and the outdoors beyond academic training and be able to demonstrate effective teaching skills and the ability to contribute to high-quality instruction, as well as provide practical applications within their area of expertise. Strong interpersonal and communication skills as well as the ability to work effectively and collegially with faculty, staff, and students will be key. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to contribute to curriculum development, instructional innovation, student mentoring, and other activities that support the teaching mission of the department and school, as appropriate to their assigned responsibilities. Candidates requesting appointment at the Senior Lecturer or Teaching Professor rank must demonstrate teaching experience and accomplishments appropriate to the proposed rank. Department Contact for Questions Questions about the PeopleAdmin application procedure may be directed to Dave Archer at dwarcher@iu.edu . Questions regarding the position may be directed to Lisa Koontz, Director of Faculty Operations, lmkoontz@iu.edu , or Grace Sembajwe, Executive Associate Dean, gsembajw@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Application Procedure: Please provide (1) a curriculum vitae and (2) a cover letter no longer than five pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, including a statement of your teaching interests, experience, and approach to supporting student learning. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34585 For Best Consideration Date 12/14/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101721-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 2 Other 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34732": {
