blic Health‐Bloomington (SPH‐B) invites applications for the position of Lecturer of Tourism, Hospitality, and Event Management in the Department of Sport Management, Tourism, & Recreation. This 10-month appointment would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by December 14, 2026 , will receive full priority consideration, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Responsibilities: As non-tenure-track faculty, Lecturers are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of the department through excellence in teaching and student learning; developing, delivering, and enhancing courses and curricula within their areas of expertise; mentoring and supporting undergraduate and/or graduate students as appropriate; engaging in professional development and scholarly or creative activities that support teaching and student learning. This role is comprised of primarily teaching in tourism, hospitality, and event management but will also be expected to contribute as a generalist to larger departmental needs. About IUB : Founded in 1820, Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University and has been a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909. Indiana University Bloomington prides itself in offering outstanding academics grounded in world class research and vibrant campus life. Located in Bloomington, IN, IUB strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. Indiana University Bloomington is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. The campus enrolls more than 48,000 students and is home to 16 degree-granting schools and colleges. IU Bloomington offers more than 200 undergraduate majors as well as extensive graduate and professional study opportunities, including more than 90 master’s degrees and more than 80 Ph.D. programs. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IU Bloomington is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. For more information about Indiana University Bloomington, visit https://bloomington.iu.edu/ . About SPH -B: The School of Public Health-Bloomington ( SPH -B) is located in the heart of the Bloomington campus and comprises five collaborative academic departments with 300 faculty and staff. Indiana University provides IU SPH -B faculty outstanding teaching and research support through programs like the Faculty Academy on Excellence in Teaching (F.A.C.E.T.); extensive research development and research administrative support through the Office of the Vice President for Research; and innovative collaborations with organizations such as the NCAA , the Indianapolis Colts, Indiana University Athletic Department, the US National Park Service, and a wealth of local, national, and international partners to broaden the scope of the faculty and student experience. SPH -B continues its rapid expansion embracing a comprehensive and holistic approach to promoting health and wellbeing within the research, teaching, and service aspects of our mission. With an emphasis on high-quality, impactful research, excellence in teaching, and meaningful service, there has never been a more exciting time to join our growing and evolving team. For more information about the School of Public Health – Bloomington, visit https://www.publichealth.indiana.edu/ . About Bloomington: Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. For more information about Bloomington, IN, visit https://www.visitbloomington.com/ . Basic Qualifications Qualifications: Candidates must hold a master’s degree or higher, with a preference given to those holding a doctoral degree, in Tourism, Hospitality, or Event Management, or a closely related field from a reputable, well-established institution. Candidates must have experience in the field of Tourism, Hospitality, and Event Management beyond academic training and be able to demonstrate effective teaching skills and the ability to contribute to high-quality instruction in their area of expertise. Strong interpersonal and communication skills as well as the ability to work effectively and collegially with faculty, staff, and students will be key. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to contribute to curriculum development, instructional innovation, student mentoring, and other activities that support the teaching mission of the department and school, as appropriate to their assigned responsibilities. Candidates requesting appointment at the Senior Lecturer or Teaching Professor rank must demonstrate teaching experience and accomplishments appropriate to the proposed rank. Department Contact for Questions Questions about the PeopleAdmin application procedure may be directed to Dave Archer at dwarcher@iu.edu . Questions regarding the position may be directed to Lisa Koontz, Director of Faculty Operations, lmkoontz@iu.edu , or Grace Sembajwe, Executive Associate Dean, gsembajw@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Application Procedure: Please provide (1) a curriculum vitae and (2) a cover letter no longer than five pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, including a statement of your teaching interests, experience, and approach to supporting student learning. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34592 . For Best Consideration Date 12/14/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101723-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 2 Other 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
