    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34731": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Biostatistics",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant or Associate Professor of Biostatistics Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant or Associate Professor of Biostatistics Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Procedure: Please provide a (1) curriculum vitae and (2) cover letter no longer than 5 pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, which includes a research statement and overview of research experience, and a statement of teaching interest and experience. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34343 . Before a conditional offer of employment is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Biostatistics Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Epidemiology and Biostatistics Location Bloomington Position Summary The Indiana University School of Public Health‐Bloomington (SPH‐B) invites applications for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor of Biostatistics in the Department of Epidemiology and Biostatistics. This 10-month appointment would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by November 1, 2026 , will receive full priority consideration, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The SPH -B seeks individuals who will contribute to scientific and academic excellence through rigorous research, teaching, and service in biostatistics with special emphasis on the machine learning and artificial intelligence, while advancing interdisciplinary collaboration and the development and application of evidence to improve public health. A member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) prides itself in offering outstanding academics grounded in world class research and vibrant campus life. The School of Public Health-Bloomington is located on the flagship campus of Indiana University in Bloomington, IN and is composed of over 160 faculty across five departments. The Department of Epidemiology and Biostatistics advances public health through the study of the distribution and patterns of health events and the development and application of statistical methods to human health research. The department offers a Bachelor of Science in Public Health (B.S.P.H.) in Epidemiology, a Master of Public Health (M.P.H.) in Epidemiology, a Master of Science (M.S.) in Biostatistics, a Ph.D. in Epidemiology, and a Ph.D. in Biostatistics. Faculty conduct research across a broad range of health outcomes and exposures and prepare students for careers in academia, industry, government, health agencies, and other research settings. The department also houses the Biostatistics Consulting Center, which provides study design and data analysis expertise for health-related research and supports interdisciplinary research collaborations across Indiana University and beyond. Responsibilities: Tenure-track faculty are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of the department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research in modern public health science both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; teaching and mentoring students at the undergraduate and/or graduate level as designated by the department chairperson; and actively providing service internally to the department, school and university and externally to the profession and/or the community.Areas of special interest include, but are not limited to modern machine learning methods, artificial intelligence (AI), high-dimensional data analysis and novel clinical trials design. About IUB : Founded in 1820, Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN, IU Bloomington constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. Indiana University Bloomington is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. The campus enrolls more than 48,000 students and is home to 16 degree-granting schools and colleges. IU Bloomington offers more than 200 undergraduate majors as well as extensive graduate and professional study opportunities, including more than 90 master’s degrees and more than 80 Ph.D. programs. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IU Bloomington is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. For more information about Indiana University Bloomington, visit https://bloomington.iu.edu/ . About SPH -B: The School of Public Health-Bloomington ( SPH -B) is located in the heart of the Bloomington campus and comprises five collaborative academic departments with 300 faculty and staff. Indiana University provides IU SPH -B faculty outstanding teaching and research support through programs like the Faculty Academy on Excellence in Teaching (F.A.C.E.T.); extensive research development and research administrative support through the Office of the Vice President for Research; and innovative collaborations with organizations such as the Indianapolis Colts, Indiana University Athletic Department, US National Park Service, and a wealth of local, national, and international partners to broaden the scope of the faculty and student experience. SPH -B continues its rapid expansion embracing a comprehensive and holistic approach to promoting health and wellbeing within the research, teaching, and service aspects of our mission. With an emphasis on high-quality, impactful research, excellence in teaching, and meaningful service, there has never been a more exciting time to join our growing and evolving team. For more information about the School of Public Health – Bloomington, visit https://www.publichealth.indiana.edu/ . About Bloomington: Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. For more information about Bloomington, IN, visit https://www.visitbloomington.com/ . Basic Qualifications Candidates must hold a doctorate degree in Biostatistics, Statistics or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Candidates must have teaching experience at the graduate or professional level. Good interpersonal skills, effective communication skills, and the ability to work cooperatively and congenially across disciplines are required. Leadership skills and vision for enhancing the academic components of an interdisciplinary department are essential. Candidates for associate and full professor positions must also demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for a senior career level, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Department Contact for Questions Questions about the PeopleAdmin application procedure may be directed to Dave Archer at dwarcher@iu.edu . Questions regarding the position may be directed to Lisa Koontz, Director of Faculty Operations, lmkoontz@iu.edu , or Grace Sembajwe, Executive Associate Dean, gsembajw@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Application Procedure: Please provide a (1) curriculum vitae and (2) cover letter no longer than 5 pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, which includes a research statement and overview of research experience, and a statement of teaching interest and experience. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34343 . Before a conditional offer of employment is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101681-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 2 Other 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34730": {
      "title": "Chair and Tenured Faculty Position Department of Sport Management, Tourism, and Recreation",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Chair and Tenured Faculty Position Department of Sport Management, Tourism, and Recreation Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Chair and Tenured Faculty Position Department of Sport Management, Tourism, and Recreation Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Procedure: Please provide a (1) curriculum vitae and (2) cover letter no longer than 5 pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, which includes a research statement and overview of research experience, and a statement of teaching interest and experience. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references; references will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34358 Before a conditional offer of employment is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Posting Details Position Details Title Chair and Tenured Faculty Position Department of Sport Management, Tourism, and Recreation Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington School of Public Health Location Bloomington Position Summary The Indiana University School of Public Health‐Bloomington (SPH‐B) invites applications for the position of Chair and Tenured Professor in the Department of Sport Management, Tourism, and Recreation. We are seeking an accomplished and collaborative leader with a strong record of research, academic leadership, and administration who is excited by the opportunity to shape the future of a newly formed department and champion the success of its faculty, staff, and students. We seek candidates who bring multidisciplinary perspectives, intellectual curiosity, and a commitment to excellence in research, teaching, service, and mentorship. The successful candidate will help advance an ambitious vision for a department positioned at the intersection of sport, tourism, recreation, health, and human well-being. This 12-month appointment would ideally start July 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by November 30, 2026 , will receive full priority consideration, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. This position presents a rare opportunity to lead a newly formed department with established strengths, outstanding faculty, and strong momentum. The next chair will play a pivotal role in shaping the department’s identity, fostering interdisciplinary collaboration, expanding its impact, and advancing excellence across its teaching, research, and service missions. A member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, Indiana University Bloomington prides itself in offering outstanding academics grounded in world-class research and vibrant campus life. The School of Public Health-Bloomington, located on the university’s flagship campus, includes more than 160 faculty members across five departments. The newly formed Department of Sport Management, Tourism, and Recreation maintains strong connections across the School of Public Health-Bloomington and throughout Indiana University. Although newly formed, the department brings together established programs with more than 80 years of collective history and accomplishment. Given robust enrollment growth, SPH -B has recently been engaged in a major faculty hiring initiative and is launching another wave of faculty recruitment, including this search for an innovative and visionary chair who will help define the department’s next chapter and elevate its national and international impact. Responsibilities: The chair will provide inspirational and practical leadership for research, teaching, and service; manage the budget and secure financial resources to meet program objectives; actively assist with fundraising activities; represent the department on external committees and to groups; oversee operations of the department’s undergraduate and graduate teaching including the recruitment and mentorship of outstanding faculty, staff, and students; and facilitate productive interaction among faculty, staff, students, and alumni. It is expected that the successful candidate will work closely with the dean to further the school’s goals and mission related to teaching, research, and service. About Indiana University Bloomington: Founded in 1820, Indiana University Bloomington is the flagship campus of Indiana University and a member of the Association of American Universities ( AAU ). With more than 47,000 students and a strong tradition of excellence in research, teaching, and service, IU Bloomington provides an exceptional environment for academic innovation and collaboration. The School of Public Health-Bloomington includes five academic departments, with more than 300 faculty and staff, and a shared commitment to advancing health and well-being through impactful research, education, and community engagement. Indiana University provides SPH -B faculty with exceptional support for teaching and research through programs such as the Faculty Academy on Excellence in Teaching (F.A.C.E.T.), extensive research development and administrative support through the Office of the Vice President for Research, and collaborations with organizations including the NCAA , Indianapolis Colts, Indiana University Athletics, the U.S. National Park Service, and a wealth of local, national, and international partners. Together, these resources create an environment that fosters innovation, interdisciplinary collaboration, and meaningful scholarly impact. Located in south-central Indiana, Bloomington combines the vibrancy of a major research university with the quality of life of a welcoming college town, offering a rich arts scene, outstanding outdoor recreation, excellent schools, and a reasonable cost of living. For more information about the School of Public Health-Bloomington and Indiana University Bloomington, visit: School of Public Health-Bloomington: http://www.publichealth.indiana.edu Indiana University Bloomington: https://www.indiana.edu Basic Qualifications Qualifications: Candidates must hold a doctoral degree in a closely related ﬁeld within sport management, recreation, tourism management, and/or recreational therapy . A background through education and/or experience in public health will be seen as an advantage in this role. Candidates must also demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for a senior career level, including evidence of high-quality teaching, research, and curriculum development. The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to build consensus, inspire excellence, foster a positive culture, and bring people together around a shared vision for the department’s future. The candidate is expected to be appointed as a tenured professor. Finally, candidates are expected to reside in Bloomington, Indiana, to permit full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Department Contact for Questions Questions about the PeopleAdmin application procedure may be directed to Dave Archer at dwarcher@iu.edu or via postal mail at Department of Sport Management, Tourism, and Recreation Search & Screen Committee, School Public Health–Bloomington, Indiana University, 1025 East 7th Street, Bloomington, IN 47405-4801. Questions regarding the position may be directed to Lisa Koontz, Director of Faculty Operations, lmkoontz@iu.edu , or Grace Sembajwe, Executive Associate Dean, gsembajw@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Application Procedure: Please provide a (1) curriculum vitae and (2) cover letter no longer than 5 pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, which includes a research statement and overview of research experience, and a statement of teaching interest and experience. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references; references will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34358 Before a conditional offer of employment is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. For Best Consideration Date 11/30/2026 Expected Start Date 07/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101686-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 2 Other 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34728": {
      "title": "Department Chair and Tenured Faculty Position Department of Kinesiology",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Department Chair and Tenured Faculty Position Department of Kinesiology Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Department Chair and Tenured Faculty Position Department of Kinesiology Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Procedure: Please provide (1) a curriculum vitae (CV) and (2) a cover letter (4 pages maximum) summarizing key qualifications and reasons for interest in the position. The cover letter should address your leadership experience and vision for the department; research and scholarly accomplishments, including experience with externally funded research; teaching and mentoring experience; and relevant experience in academic administration, faculty and staff development, academic programs and curricula, research leadership, budget and resource management, and communication and collaboration. Finalists will be asked to provide six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34414 . Misconduct Disclosure: Before a conditional offer of employment is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by IUB with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by IUB on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that IUB takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Posting Details Position Details Title Department Chair and Tenured Faculty Position Department of Kinesiology Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Kinesiology Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) School of Public Health‐Bloomington (SPH‐B) invites applications for the position of Department Chair and Tenured Professor in the Department of Kinesiology. The SPH -B seeks an accomplished academic leader who will provide leadership, vision, and strategic and practical direction for the Department of Kinesiology to advance excellence in research, teaching, and service related to exercise, physical activity, and all aspects of human movement and performance, broadly defined. This 12-month appointment would ideally start July 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by November 18, 2026 , will receive full priority consideration, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. This position is located on the Bloomington campus of Indiana University. Successful candidates are expected to work on campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, university, and community. Indiana University bases tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in research, teaching, and service. A successful candidate will foster the continued development and success of the department’s faculty and staff, academic programs and students, research enterprise, and outreach programs while strengthening interdisciplinary collaborations and leveraging opportunities to advance knowledge and its application to health and well-being. This position represents a unique opportunity to lead a department with 75+ years of outstanding legacy yet one that is also uniquely well-positioned for excellence within a school of public health, especially with our recently acquired new leadership. Responsibilities: The Department Chair provides leadership, vision, and strategic direction for the department and is responsible for advancing excellence across its academic, research, and service missions. The Chair also provides general administration and oversight of departmental operations; promotes the recruitment, development, success, and retention of faculty and staff; supports student academic and professional success; and provides leadership for the development, delivery, assessment, and continuous improvement of academic programs and curricula. The Chair fosters a strong research environment, supports faculty scholarship and the pursuit of external funding, and facilitates interdisciplinary and collaborative research within the SPH -B, across IUB and IU more broadly, and with external partners. The Chair is responsible for effective stewardship of the department’s budget, resources, and funding priorities and works to identify opportunities that support the department’s strategic goals and continued growth. The Chair promotes effective, transparent, and timely communication within the department and serves as an advocate and representative for the department to the school, university, profession, and broader community. Beyond administrative responsibilities, the Chair is expected to maintain an active research program with scholarship, contribute to teaching/mentoring, and provide service aligned with an appointment as Professor. About Kinesiology : As a legacy program on the IUB campus, the Department of Kinesiology, with 30 full-time faculty, has a strong and growing enrollment in the undergraduate Exercise Science degree program (~1,375 students), and healthy enrollments in graduate degree programs (~75 students) including an MS in Athletic Training, MS in Kinesiology, and a PhD in Human Performance. Faculty conduct research across numerous areas including exercise physiology (with historical excellence in environmental and clinical exercise physiology), biomechanics, neuromuscular/motor control, physical activity and fitness interventions, athletic training, and sport-based approaches to health and well-being. Kinesiology faculty are active contributors to the SPH -B Nutrition and Exercise Research Center and collaborate with the Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences and the related Imaging Research Facility . An emerging exemplar of community engagement, Hoosier Sport, a growing research and experiential learning outreach program that serves surrounding communities, uses sport to promote physical activity, health, leadership, and positive youth development. Finally, the department supports the Physical Activity Instruction Program, an extensive fitness and sport focused academic service program. About SPH -B : The SPH -B is in the heart of the Bloomington campus and comprises five collaborative academic departments with 300 faculty and staff. With recent rapid growth in both enrollments (~4,600 total students, ~470 graduate students) and 160 faculty, the SPH -B is well positioned for the challenges and opportunities of contemporary higher education. In addition to a robust administrative infrastructure, notable SPH -B faculty support units include an exceptional Grants Administration Office, talented Office of Online Education, and a creative Marketing & Communications team. IUB also provides SPH -B faculty outstanding teaching support through programs like the Faculty Academy on Excellence in Teaching (F.A.C.E.T.); extensive research development and research administrative support through the Office of the Vice President for Research; and innovative collaborations with organizations such as the NCAA , Indianapolis Colts, Indiana University Athletics, the U.S. National Park Service, and a wealth of local, national, and international partners to broaden the scope of the faculty and student experience. SPH -B continues its rapid expansion, embracing a comprehensive and holistic approach to promoting health and wellbeing within the research, teaching, and service aspects of our mission. With an emphasis on high-quality, impactful research, excellence in teaching and mentoring, and meaningful and impactful service, there has never been a more exciting time to join our growing and evolving team. About IUB : Founded in 1820, Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University and is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. A member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, IUB prides itself in offering outstanding academics grounded in world class research and a vibrant campus life with 48,000+ students and 16 degree-granting schools and colleges. IUB offers 200+ undergraduate majors as well as extensive graduate and professional study opportunities, including 90+ master’s degrees and 80+ Ph.D. programs. IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is considered by many to be one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. About Bloomington : Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. Basic Qualifications Qualifications: Candidates must hold a doctoral degree in kinesiology, exercise/movement science , or a closely related field from an accredited institution and possess a record of scholarly achievement, teaching, and service appropriate for appointment as a senior faculty member at IUB . Candidates must possess a distinguished record of research and scholarship, including success in securing extramural funding and experience leading significant research initiatives. Evidence of effective teaching and mentoring at the undergraduate and/or graduate level is required with curriculum experience preferred. Candidates must possess leadership experience and evidence of the ability to build consensus and articulate, build and advance a compelling vision for the department; effectively administer academic programs, personnel, and resources including budgets; support the professional development and success of faculty and staff; promote student academic and professional success; and foster excellence and innovation across the tri-partite mission of teaching, research and service. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, sound judgment, and the ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and build productive relationships is essential. Finally, and importantly, the successful candidate must be able to foster a positive work culture and coalesce the department toward future excellence. Department Contact for Questions Questions: · Questions about the PeopleAdmin application procedure may be directed to Dave Archer at dwarcher@iu.edu . · Questions regarding the position may be directed to Lisa Koontz, Director of Faculty Operations, lmkoontz@iu.edu , or Grace Sembajwe, Executive Associate Dean, gsembajw@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Application Procedure: Please provide (1) a curriculum vitae (CV) and (2) a cover letter (4 pages maximum) summarizing key qualifications and reasons for interest in the position. The cover letter should address your leadership experience and vision for the department; research and scholarly accomplishments, including experience with externally funded research; teaching and mentoring experience; and relevant experience in academic administration, faculty and staff development, academic programs and curricula, research leadership, budget and resource management, and communication and collaboration. Finalists will be asked to provide six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34414 . Misconduct Disclosure: Before a conditional offer of employment is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by IUB with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by IUB on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that IUB takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. For Best Consideration Date 11/18/2026 Expected Start Date 07/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101696-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 2 Other 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34727": {
      "title": "Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Digital Media, Behavior Change, &amp; Public Health Department of Applied Health Science",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Digital Media, Behavior Change, &amp; Public Health Department of Applied Health Science Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Digital Media, Behavior Change, & Public Health Department of Applied Health Science Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Procedure: Please provide a (1) curriculum vitae and (2) cover letter no longer than 5 pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, which includes a research statement and overview of research experience, and a statement of teaching interest and experience. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34468 . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Posting Details Position Details Title Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Digital Media, Behavior Change, & Public Health Department of Applied Health Science Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Applied Health Science Location Bloomington Position Summary The Indiana University School of Public Health‐Bloomington (SPH‐B) invites applications for a Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Digital Media, Behavior Change, & Public Health in the Department of Applied Health Science. The SPH -B seeks individuals who will contribute to academic excellence in research, teaching, and service in support of the Department of Applied Health Science’s mission to prevent disease and promote the health and well-being of individuals, families, and communities. This 10-month appointment would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by 11/1/2026 will receive full priority consideration, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Responsibilities: Tenured/Tenure-track faculty are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of the department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research in modern public health science both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; teaching and mentoring students at the undergraduate and/or graduate level as designated by the department chairperson; and actively providing service internally to the department, school and university and externally to the profession and/or the community. Areas of interest include examining how social media, digital environments, and emerging technologies influence health behaviors and outcomes among youth and young adults, as well as developing and evaluating digital interventions to prevent or address health risks and conditions such as tobacco use, diabetes, obesity, physical inactivity, and injury. Related areas of interest may include digital health, health communication, behavior change, and technology-enabled approaches to promoting health and well-being. About IUB : Founded in 1820, Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University and has been a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909. Indiana University Bloomington prides itself in offering outstanding academics grounded in world class research and vibrant campus life. Located in Bloomington, IN, IUB strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. Indiana University Bloomington is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. The campus enrolls more than 48,000 students and is home to 16 degree-granting schools and colleges. IU Bloomington offers more than 200 undergraduate majors as well as extensive graduate and professional study opportunities, including more than 90 master’s degrees and more than 80 Ph.D. programs. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IU Bloomington is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. For more information about Indiana University Bloomington, visit https://bloomington.iu.edu/ . About SPH -B: The School of Public Health-Bloomington ( SPH -B) is located in the heart of the Bloomington campus and comprises five collaborative academic departments with 300 faculty and staff. Indiana University provides IU SPH -B faculty outstanding teaching and research support through programs like the Faculty Academy on Excellence in Teaching (F.A.C.E.T.); extensive research development and research administrative support through the Office of the Vice President for Research; and innovative collaborations with organizations such as the NCAA , the Indianapolis Colts, Indiana University Athletic Department, the US National Park Service, and a wealth of local, national, and international partners to broaden the scope of the faculty and student experience. SPH -B continues its rapid expansion embracing a comprehensive and holistic approach to promoting health and wellbeing within the research, teaching, and service aspects of our mission. With an emphasis on high-quality, impactful research, excellence in teaching, and meaningful service, there has never been a more exciting time to join our growing and evolving team. For more information about the School of Public Health – Bloomington, visit https://www.publichealth.indiana.edu/ . About Bloomington: Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. For more information about Bloomington, IN, visit https://www.visitbloomington.com/ . Basic Qualifications Qualifications: Candidates must hold a doctorate degree in public health, behavioral or social science, health communication, psychology, health informatics, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Candidates must have teaching experience at the graduate or professional level. Excellent interpersonal skills, effective communication skills, and the ability to work cooperatively and congenially across disciplines are required. Leadership skills and vision for enhancing the academic components of an interdisciplinary department are essential. Candidates for associate and full professor positions must also demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for a senior career level, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. This position is part of Indiana University Bloomington’s interdisciplinary Shaping Health Through Media: Trauma, Technology, and Society faculty cluster, which brings together scholars across public health, media and communication, psychological and behavioral sciences, education, and technology. The successful candidate will have opportunities to develop interdisciplinary collaborations focused on understanding how media and emerging technologies shape health and well-being and how these environments can be leveraged to improve health outcomes. Department Contact for Questions Questions about the PeopleAdmin application procedure may be directed to Dave Archer at dwarcher@iu.edu . Questions regarding the position may be directed to Lisa Koontz, Director of Faculty Operations, lmkoontz@iu.edu , or Grace Sembajwe, Executive Associate Dean, gsembajw@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Application Procedure: Please provide a (1) curriculum vitae and (2) cover letter no longer than 5 pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, which includes a research statement and overview of research experience, and a statement of teaching interest and experience. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34468 . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. For Best Consideration Date 11/01/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101700-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 3 Research Paper 1 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34726": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Sport Management Department of Sport Management, Tourism, &amp; Recreation",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Lecturer of Sport Management Department of Sport Management, Tourism, &amp; Recreation Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Lecturer of Sport Management Department of Sport Management, Tourism, & Recreation Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Procedure: Please provide (1) a curriculum vitae and (2) a cover letter no longer than five pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, including a statement of your teaching interests, experience, and approach to supporting student learning. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34596 . Posting Details Position Details Title Lecturer of Sport Management Department of Sport Management, Tourism, & Recreation Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington School of Public Health Location Bloomington Position Summary The Indiana University School of Public Health‐Bloomington (SPH‐B) invites applications for the position of Lecturer of Sport Marketing and Management in the Department of Sport Management, Tourism, & Recreation. This 10-month appointment would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by December 14, 2026 , will receive full priority consideration, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Responsibilities: As non-tenure-track faculty, Lecturers are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of the department through excellence in teaching and student learning; developing, delivering, and enhancing courses and curricula within their areas of expertise; mentoring and supporting undergraduate and/or graduate students as appropriate; engaging in professional development and scholarly or creative activities that support teaching and student learning. This role will primarily involve teaching courses in sport marketing and management, while also contributing as a generalist to broader departmental teaching and curricular needs. About IUB : Founded in 1820, Indiana University Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University and has been a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909. Indiana University Bloomington prides itself in offering outstanding academics grounded in world class research and vibrant campus life. Located in Bloomington, IN, IUB strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. Indiana University Bloomington is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. The campus enrolls more than 48,000 students and is home to 16 degree-granting schools and colleges. IU Bloomington offers more than 200 undergraduate majors as well as extensive graduate and professional study opportunities, including more than 90 master’s degrees and more than 80 Ph.D. programs. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IU Bloomington is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. For more information about Indiana University Bloomington, visit https://bloomington.iu.edu/ . About SPH -B: The School of Public Health-Bloomington ( SPH -B) is located in the heart of the Bloomington campus and comprises five collaborative academic departments with 300 faculty and staff. Indiana University provides IU SPH -B faculty outstanding teaching and research support through programs like the Faculty Academy on Excellence in Teaching (F.A.C.E.T.); extensive research development and research administrative support through the Office of the Vice President for Research; and innovative collaborations with organizations such as the NCAA , the Indianapolis Colts, Indiana University Athletic Department, the US National Park Service, and a wealth of local, national, and international partners to broaden the scope of the faculty and student experience. SPH -B continues its rapid expansion embracing a comprehensive and holistic approach to promoting health and wellbeing within the research, teaching, and service aspects of our mission. With an emphasis on high-quality, impactful research, excellence in teaching, and meaningful service, there has never been a more exciting time to join our growing and evolving team. For more information about the School of Public Health – Bloomington, visit https://www.publichealth.indiana.edu/ . About Bloomington: Nestled in the rolling hills of south-central Indiana, and home to 85,000 residents, the city of Bloomington offers the feel of a college town with many of the amenities of a large city. From off-Broadway plays and musicals, the LOTUS World Festival of Music, quick access to 250,000 acres of public recreation lands, outstanding public schools and a reasonable cost of living, Bloomington offers much to all. For more information about Bloomington, IN, visit https://www.visitbloomington.com/ . Basic Qualifications Qualifications: Candidates must hold a master’s degree or higher, with a preference given to those holding a doctoral degree, in Sport Management or a closely related field from a reputable, well-established institution. Candidates must have experience in the field of Sport Management beyond academic training and be able to demonstrate effective teaching skills and the ability to contribute to high-quality instruction in their area of expertise. Strong interpersonal and communication skills as well as the ability to work effectively and collegially with faculty, staff, and students will be key. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to contribute to curriculum development, instructional innovation, student mentoring, and other activities that support the teaching mission of the department and school, as appropriate to their assigned responsibilities. Candidates requesting appointment at the Senior Lecturer or Teaching Professor rank must demonstrate teaching experience and accomplishments appropriate to the proposed rank. Department Contact for Questions Questions about the PeopleAdmin application procedure may be directed to Dave Archer at dwarcher@iu.edu . Questions regarding the position may be directed to Lisa Koontz, Director of Faculty Operations, lmkoontz@iu.edu , or Grace Sembajwe, Executive Associate Dean, gsembajw@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Application Procedure: Please provide (1) a curriculum vitae and (2) a cover letter no longer than five pages in length summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position, including a statement of your teaching interests, experience, and approach to supporting student learning. If selected as a finalist, we will additionally request a list of up to six (6) references. References will be contacted if you are selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34596 . For Best Consideration Date 12/14/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101724-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 2 Other 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34722": {
      "title": "Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in AI-Enabled Experiments for Scientific Discovery in Health",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in AI-Enabled Experiments for Scientific Discovery in Health Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in AI-Enabled Experiments for Scientific Discovery in Health Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Open Rank, Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Position in AI-Enabled Experiments for Scientific Discovery in Health Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Vice Provost For Faculty Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary Indiana University Bloomington invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor or tenured associate or full professor in the Department of Statistics, College of Arts and Sciences. We seek an outstanding researcher to develop a research program at the forefront of statistics, artificial intelligence, experimentation, and health. AI systems now participate not only in analyzing data but in designing experiments, selecting interventions, and guiding scientific discovery. This shift calls for new statistical foundations, and this opening offers a well-resourced professorship to build a research program that develops these foundations. We are especially interested in candidates developing statistical methodology for AI-enabled experimentation in health, aging, and related areas. Relevant settings include: autonomous and AI-guided experimentation adaptive and innovative clinical trials precision medicine self-driving laboratories digital twins and in-silico experimentation AI-enabled drug discovery. Regulatory frameworks are evolving alongside these developments, including recent FDA guidance on credible, validated applications of AI, model-informed approaches and new experimental methodologies in drug development. Exceptional candidates in other application areas will also be considered. We welcome candidates whose research develops methodology and theory in a variety of subfields of statistics relevant to AI-enabled experimentation, including: experimental design, clinical trial design, and sequential experimentation Bayesian optimization and active learning contextual bandits, reinforcement learning and online experimentation causal inference and treatment-effect heterogeneity statistical learning and machine learning evaluation and monitoring of AI systems micro-randomized trials uncertainty quantification prediction-powered inference. Indiana University Bloomington offers an unusually rich environment for this research. IU has established major academic-industry partnerships in health and biotechnology, including a five-year $40M partnership with Eli Lilly on AI-enabled clinical trials research, and a five-year master collaboration agreement with Cook Medical. These partnerships are coordinated through the IU Launch Accelerator for Biosciences and complement IU’s clinical and health-science ecosystem, including the IU Medical Center and IU School of Medicine, giving faculty the opportunity to work across the full span from statistical theory and methodology to applied industry collaborations and translation into practice. Located approximately one hour from Indianapolis, Bloomington provides access to one of the nation’s major health and life-sciences hubs. The successful candidate will join a collegial, research-active department with strengths in Bayesian methods, high-dimensional statistics, computational statistics, physics-informed inference, and biostatistics, and will help shape its direction in AI-enabled and health-oriented statistics. The department is closely tied to the Indiana Statistical Consulting Center, which serves researchers across the university, and has natural collaborators in the Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering, home to the Luddy Center for Artificial Intelligence and its focus on AI for digital health, as well as in the Department of Mathematics, Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences, the Cognitive Science program, and the School of Public Health-Bloomington. These 10‐month appointments would ideally start August 1, 2027 , although an earlier or later start date is negotiable. Applications received by December 1, 2026, will receive full consideration, and applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Responsibilities: Tenured/tenure-track faculty at Indiana University Bloomington are expected to substantially contribute to the overall academic excellence of their department by developing and/or maintaining a robust research portfolio including pursuing and obtaining major extramural research funding to conduct cutting-edge research both as a corresponding principal investigator and a collaborating investigator; teaching and mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students as designated by the department chairperson; and actively providing service within the department, school and university alongside active engagement with the profession and/or the community. The position is located on the campus of Indiana University, Bloomington ( IUB ) in Bloomington, Indiana, and successful candidates are expected to work on the IUB campus to allow full engagement with the department, school, campus, and community. Indiana University bases its tenure and promotion recommendations upon performance in three areas including research, teaching, and service. All individuals hired through this initiative are expected to excel in research and provide strong performance in teaching and service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in statistics (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates for w/tenure positions must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for an appointment w/tenure, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, established record of publications and scholarly work, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Application Procedures: Review of applications will begin December 1, 2026 and continue until all positions are filled. Application materials should include: Cover letter (maximum of 3 pages in length, identifying your application for a position with tenure (associate/full professor) or a tenure-track position (assistant professor), and summarize your interest in the position. Current Curriculum Vitae Research Statement (maximum of 4 pages in length) Teaching Statement (maximum of 2 pages in length) Contact information for three professional references Professional references for applicants for tenure-track positions will only be solicited for those selected for a screening interview. Professional references for applicants for positions with tenure will only be solicited for those selected for a finalist interview and/or job offer. Applicants for associate or full professor should apply at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34576 All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Nathan Glatt-Holtz ( negh@iu.edu ) , search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. About Indiana University Bloomington : Founded in 1820, Indiana University-Bloomington ( IUB ) is the flagship campus of Indiana University. Located in Bloomington, IN., IUB constantly strives to embody its mission to create, disseminate, preserve, and apply knowledge. It does so through its commitments to cutting-edge research, scholarship, arts, and creative activity; inspired and challenging undergraduate, graduate, professional, and lifelong educational programs; meaningful experiences outside the classroom; expansive global educational opportunities; first-rate library and museum collections; and far-reaching economic development and impact in the state and region. IUB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ) since 1909, is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is a member of the North Central Association. With over 47,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the campus has 16 degree-granting colleges and schools offering 300+ undergraduate majors, 300+ Master’s degrees, and 150+ doctoral and professional degree opportunities. Known for its Indiana limestone facades and green spaces throughout, IUB is widely considered one of the country’s most beautiful college campuses. More information about the Department of Statistics at Indiana University Bloomington can be found at www.stat.indiana.edu. Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should possess a PhD in statistics (or a related field) and be committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Candidates for w/tenure positions must demonstrate a record of scholarly achievement appropriate for an appointment w/tenure, including extramurally funded research as a corresponding principal investigator, current funding or strong potential to secure external funding, established record of publications and scholarly work, and experience leading sizeable research initiatives. Department Contact for Questions All queries about the position or the application procedures should be addressed to Dr. Nathan Glatt-Holtz (negh@iu.edu), search chairperson, or Dr. Cindy Broderick, search coordinator, at faculty1@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Commensurate with experience Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 12/01/2026 Expected Start Date Posting Number IU-101717-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No How did you hear about this position? Personal Contact: At Professional Meeting or Conference Personal Contact: Direct Contact by Search Committee Personal Contact: Referred by colleague or advisor Announcement: Chronicle of Higher Education Announcement: IU Bulletin for Academic Appointees Announcement: Other Journal or Magazine Announcement: Other Website Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Agenda Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34699": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow - Capone Lab - ENVR",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Postdoctoral Fellow - Capone Lab - ENVR Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Postdoctoral Fellow - Capone Lab - ENVR Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Provide CV, cover letter summarizing research interests and fit for position, writing sample, and a list of three references. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34329 . Posting Details Position Details Title Postdoctoral Fellow - Capone Lab - ENVR Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Environmental and Occupational Health Location Bloomington Position Summary A postdoctoral fellow position is available in the Capone Lab in the Department of Environmental and Occupational Health at the Indiana University School of Public Health-Bloomington. The fellow will join a multidisciplinary team conducting a five-year CDC -funded study focused on developing and applying integrated surveillance approaches for soil-transmitted helminth ( STH ) infection in the southeastern United States. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis, but applications received by October 5, 2026 will be given full consideration, and the search will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. The earliest anticipated start date is October 19, 2026. Dr. Drew Capone’s research group ( https://caponelab.publichealth.indiana.edu ) has broad interests in environmental health microbiology. Current projects include public health surveillance using fecal waste streams, microbial fate and transport, the role of infrastructure in interrupting enteric pathogen transmission, and predicting public health outcomes using quantitative microbial risk assessment. Lab members conduct field research in Mozambique and Indiana, as well as wet lab work in Bloomington, Indiana. We use tools from engineering, epidemiology, and environmental health microbiology to investigate the problems affecting low-income individuals and aim to improve public health in the communities where these people live. Basic Qualifications The postdoctoral fellow position requires a PhD in environmental health, environmental engineering, environmental science, microbiology, or a related scientific field by the time of appointment. We are looking for candidates with experience in several of the following areas (prior experience with helminths is not required): Experience with project management Experience with molecular microbiology methods (e.g., nucleic acid extraction, qPCR, dPCR) and quantitative data analysis Fieldwork experience, including environmental sampling Strong written and oral communication skills An interest in mentoring undergraduate, master’s, and Ph.D. students Department Contact for Questions Questions pertaining to the PeopleAdmin application procedure may be directed to dwarcher@iu.edu . Questions regarding the position may be directed to Dr. Capone at dscapone@iu.edu Additional Qualifications This position offers a unique opportunity to work at the intersection of environmental microbiology, parasitology, epidemiology, and public health surveillance. The project integrates human and environmental samples (i.e., wastewater, septage, soil, flies, and stool) and uses microscopy and molecular methods, including digital PCR , to investigate STH infection and transmission. The fellow will play a leading scientific role in the project while also coordinating laboratory activities and helping manage this large, collaborative study. The fellow will have opportunities to lead studies and peer-reviewed publications, develop and optimize laboratory methods, analyze complex environmental and epidemiologic data, mentor students, and develop independent research questions and proposals. The position includes collaboration with microbiologists, virologists, environmental engineers, entomologists, biologists, and epidemiologists, as well as travel to study sites in Virginia and Alabama. Opportunities may also be available to participate in other domestic and international projects in the Capone Lab. We are particularly interested in candidates who want to develop an independent research profile in environmental health microbiology and who enjoy working across laboratory, field, and quantitative research. Resources are available for conference travel, and the fellow will have access to formal training in grant writing, research ethics, rigor and reproducibility, and research management. Salary and Rank Special Instructions Provide CV, cover letter summarizing research interests and fit for position, writing sample, and a list of three references. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34329 . For Best Consideration Date 10/05/2026 Expected Start Date 10/19/2026 Posting Number IU-101679-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 2 Other 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34898": {
      "title": "Director of Language Instruction (DLI) in French as Lecturer of French",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Director of Language Instruction (DLI) in French as Lecturer of French Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Director of Language Instruction (DLI) in French as Lecturer of French Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should apply online at http://indiana.peopleadmin.com by providing a cover letter; CV; statement on teaching; contact information for three letters of reference; and a teaching portfolio with lesson plans, example syllabi for courses taught or created, teaching evaluations, teaching observation reports, and a video demonstrating their classroom teaching. Video should be sent in the form of a document (Word, PDF, etc.) with an embedded link to your video. Review of applications will begin November 01, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Queries can be sent to fritdept@iu.edu or steenbem@iu.edu. Posting Details Position Details Title Director of Language Instruction (DLI) in French as Lecturer of French Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington French and Italian Location Bloomington Position Summary Director of Language Instruction ( DLI ) in French as Lecturer of French Basic Qualifications The Department of French and Italian at Indiana University, Bloomington, invites applications for a Director of Language Instruction ( DLI ) in French as Lecturer in French, with the position starting on August 1, 2027. As DLI , the Lecturer will be responsible for managing all aspects of the basic French language program – including supervising graduate instructors – in collaboration with department faculty and the Director of Undergraduate Studies in French. We seek an individual who is committed to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate (and graduate) levels with native or near-native proficiency in French. Significant training or a degree specialization in language learning or instruction is required, along with a doctorate in French or a related discipline (such as, but not limited to, Second Language Acquisition or Pedagogy etc.). Candidates should have extensive teaching experience at the post-secondary level, along with evidence of pedagogical excellence as demonstrated by the teaching portfolio. Successful applicants will demonstrate the ability to design and implement curricula across multiple sections and levels, to engage in recruitment for the major, and to engage with high school French programs. The candidate will teach four courses per year in the French Language Program, including graduate pedagogy courses Department Contact for Questions Maria Sanchez Steenberger, Department Manager for the Department of French and Italian fritdept@iu.edu or steenbem@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Candidates should have extensive teaching experience at the post-secondary level, along with evidence of pedagogical excellence as demonstrated by the teaching portfolio. Successful applicants will demonstrate the ability to design and implement curricula across multiple sections and levels, to engage in recruitment for the major, and to engage with high school French programs. The candidate will teach four courses per year in the French Language Program, including graduate pedagogy courses. H1-B sponsorship is not available for this position Salary and Rank Special Instructions Applicants should apply online at http://indiana.peopleadmin.com by providing a cover letter; CV; statement on teaching; contact information for three letters of reference; and a teaching portfolio with lesson plans, example syllabi for courses taught or created, teaching evaluations, teaching observation reports, and a video demonstrating their classroom teaching. Video should be sent in the form of a document (Word, PDF , etc.) with an embedded link to your video. Review of applications will begin November 01, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Queries can be sent to fritdept@iu.edu or steenbem@iu.edu. For Best Consideration Date 11/30/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101735-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Evidence of Teaching Ability Statement of Teaching Philosophy Video Sample Syllabus Course Evaluation Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34894": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Postdoctoral Fellow Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Postdoctoral Fellow Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications received by October 21, 2026 will receive full consideration. However, we will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and apply online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34381 We will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Application Materials: 1) CV 2) Contact information for 2-3 references Posting Details Position Details Title Postdoctoral Fellow Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Intelligent Systems Engineering Location Bloomington Position Summary The Jiang Lab invites applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher position. The postdoctoral researcher will lead independent research projects focused on developing next-generation neurotechnology and biomedical imaging methods, with particular emphasis on optical, ultrasound, and photoacoustic technologies. Working under the supervision of Dr. Ying Jiang, the candidate will contribute to the development of innovative approaches for neural circuit interrogation while collaborating with interdisciplinary research teams and mentoring graduate and undergraduate students. This is an excellent opportunity for early-career scientists looking to develop a strong publication record and build an independent research trajectory within a highly collaborative and well-resourced environment. Responsibilities include designing and conducting experiments, developing and integrating photoacoustic and ultrasound systems, validating technologies in animal models, and performing quantitative data analysis and computational modeling. The researcher will be expected to prepare manuscripts and conference presentations, contribute to grant proposals, help establish new technical capabilities and research directions within the laboratory, and work independently while contributing to a dynamic and collaborative research environment. Basic Qualifications Required: Ph.D. in biomedical engineering, electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, applied physics, neuroscience, or a closely related field Strong record of peer-reviewed publications Substantial hands-on experience in experimental system development, instrumentation, or quantitative biomedical research Strong programming and data-analysis skills in MATLAB and/or Python Demonstrated ability to independently design experiments, troubleshoot complex technical problems, analyze data, and communicate research findings Excellent written and oral communication skills Department Contact for Questions Questions may be sent to: Dr. Ying Jiang ( jiang16@iu.edu ) Additional Qualifications Preferred Skills: Research experience in optics, ultrasound/acoustics, photoacoustics, biomedical imaging, neuromodulation, or neuroengineering, particularly experience involving the development, integration, calibration, or characterization of optical or ultrasound instrumentation. Salary and Rank Special Instructions Applications received by October 21, 2026 will receive full consideration. However, we will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and apply online at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34381 We will continue accepting applications until the position is filled. Application Materials: 1) CV 2) Contact information for 2-3 references For Best Consideration Date 10/21/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101690-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34893": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow/Synthetic Chemist; Chemistry Zaleski Lab",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Postdoctoral Fellow/Synthetic Chemist; Chemistry Zaleski Lab Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Postdoctoral Fellow/Synthetic Chemist; Chemistry Zaleski Lab Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Postdoctoral Fellow/Synthetic Chemist; Chemistry Zaleski Lab Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Chemistry Location Bloomington Position Summary Department Information: The Department of Chemistry in the College of Arts + Sciences at Indiana University, consists of a well-rounded research community with cutting-edge expertise in a wide variety of modern disciplines including analytical chemistry, organic chemistry, inorganic chemistry, physical chemistry, materials chemistry, and biochemistry. Job Summary: The Zaleski Lab in the Department of Chemistry at Indiana University is accepting applications for a postdoctoral research position. The position involves the design and synthesis of hybrid molecular and nanomaterial catalysts (see here for recent work: Accts. Chem. Res. 2019 , 52 , 1957; Chem. Sci. 2025 , 16 , 255. The desired start date is February 1, 2027, although this is flexible in-order-to accommodate the needs of outstanding candidates. The successful applicant will use a deep understanding of synthetic inorganic and organic ligand chemistry, as well as molecule preparation and purification to achieve research goals. Nanomaterial and catalysis experience is a plus but not required. Motivated applicants with a Ph.D. in any area of synthetic chemistry will be considered. A candidate with a strong background in solution-phase synthetic preparations and characterizations, as well as familiarity manipulating air- and moisture-sensitive chemicals, is ideally suited for the project. We seek to employ someone with demonstrable experience in chemical purification and characterization of starting materials and reaction products by standard techniques ( NMR , EPR , IR, Mass spectrometry, X-ray diffraction, TEM , and DFT calculations also desirable). The Zaleski Lab is a dynamic multidisciplinary laboratory environment. The successful applicant will play an integral role within our growing team and will emerge with a skill set that is equally relevant to academia and industry. Trainees receive regular guidance and feedback to ensure progress is made toward their career goals, whatever those may be. Trainees are also afforded the scheduling flexibility needed to maintain an appropriate work life balance and a safe laboratory environment. Responsibilities: 1. Manage own academic research and administrative activities. This involves small scale project management and coordinating multiple aspects of work to meet deadlines. 2. Train graduate and undergraduate students in research methods 3. Adapt existing, and develop new, scientific techniques and experimental protocols to achieve research objectives. 4. Use specialist scientific equipment in a laboratory environment. 5. Assist in maintaining a research laboratory (e.g. setting up Schlenk lines, ordering equipment etc.) 6. Contribute ideas for new research projects. 7. Undertake comprehensive and systematic literature reviews and write up the results for publication in peer-reviewed journals. 8. Collaborate in the preparation of scientific reports and journal articles and occasionally present papers and posters. 9. Act as a source of information and advice to other members of the group on scientific protocols and experimental techniques. 10. Represent the research group at external meetings/seminars, either with other members of the group or alone. 11. Carry out collaborative projects with colleagues in partner institutions, and research groups. Basic Qualifications Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in Chemistry Preferred Qualifications: Experience with inorganic and organic ligand synthesis and relevant analytical techniques ( NMR , EPR , SXRD , mass- spectrometry etc.) is essential. The preferred candidate will have a deep understanding of organic and/or inorganic synthesis. Department Contact for Questions Department Contact for Questions: Questions regarding the position or application process can be directed to: Prof. Jeff Zaleski, Department of Chemistry, Indiana University, 800 E. Kirkwood Avenue, Bloomington, IN 47405, zaleski@iu.edu. Salary and Rank: $52,000/year, Postdoctoral Fellow Special Instructions: The initial appointment for this position will be for 12 months. Additional 12-month extension will be available based on performance. A competitive salary along with a benefits package will be offered. Interested candidates should submit a cover letter with up to 5-page research proposal maximum , CV, and contact information for three references to https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34698 . Applications will be reviewed upon receipt. \"Indiana University is an equal employment and affirmative action employer and a provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 12/15/2026 Expected Start Date 02/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101745-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34892": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow/Biomaterials Scientist, Chemistry Zaleski Lab",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Postdoctoral Fellow/Biomaterials Scientist, Chemistry Zaleski Lab Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Postdoctoral Fellow/Biomaterials Scientist, Chemistry Zaleski Lab Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Postdoctoral Fellow/Biomaterials Scientist, Chemistry Zaleski Lab Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Chemistry Location Bloomington Position Summary Department Information: The Department of Chemistry in the College of Arts + Sciences at Indiana University, consists of a well-rounded research community with cutting-edge expertise in a wide variety of modern disciplines including analytical chemistry, organic chemistry, inorganic chemistry, physical chemistry, materials chemistry, and biochemistry. Job Summary: The Zaleski Lab in the Department of Chemistry at Indiana University is accepting applications for a postdoctoral research position. The position involves the design and synthesis of hybrid molecular and nanomaterial catalysts (see here for recent work: Accts. Chem. Res. 2019 , 52 , 1957; ACS Appl. Biomater. 2026 , 9(10), 4520; Chem. Sci. 2025 , 16 , 255. The desired start date is January 15, 2027, although this is flexible in-order-to accommodate the needs of outstanding candidates. The successful applicant will have marked experience in bacterial cell growth, management and analysis, as well as considerable expertise in membrane biochemistry and especially extracellular vesicles to achieve research goals. Working knowledge of nanomaterial preparation and interaction with cell is a strong positive. Motivated applicants with a Ph.D. in any relevant biomaterials area are strongly encouraged to apply. Candidates with a strong background in vesicle preparation, analysis, cell interactions and capabilities in advanced microscopy methods ( TEM , Confocal, light microscopy) are highly desired. The Zaleski Lab is a dynamic multidisciplinary laboratory environment. The successful applicant will play an integral role within our growing team and will emerge with a skill set that is equally relevant to academia and industry. Trainees receive regular guidance and feedback to ensure progress is made toward their career goals, whatever those may be. Trainees are also afforded the scheduling flexibility needed to maintain an appropriate work life balance and a safe laboratory environment. Responsibilities: 1. Manage own academic research and administrative activities. This involves small scale project management and coordinating multiple aspects of work to meet deadlines. 2. Train graduate and undergraduate students in research methods 3. Adapt existing, and develop new, scientific techniques and experimental protocols to achieve research objectives. 4. Use specialist scientific equipment in a laboratory environment. 5. Assist in maintaining a research laboratory (e.g. setting up new assays, ordering equipment etc.) 6. Contribute ideas for new research projects. 7. Undertake comprehensive and systematic literature reviews and write up the results for publication in peer-reviewed journals. 8. Collaborate in the preparation of scientific reports and journal articles and occasionally present papers and posters. 9. Act as a source of information and advice to other members of the group on scientific protocols and experimental techniques. 10. Represent the research group at external meetings/seminars, either with other members of the group or alone. 11. Carry out collaborative projects with colleagues in partner institutions and research groups. Basic Qualifications Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biomaterials related field Preferred Qualifications: Experience with bacterial biochemistry, membrane biology, analysis methods and microscopy related to both cells and nanomaterials is required. The preferred candidate will have a deep understanding of preparation of extracellular vesicles and cell membrane/organelle interactions. Department Contact for Questions Department Contact for Questions: Questions regarding the position or application process can be directed to: Prof. Jeff Zaleski, Department of Chemistry, Indiana University, 800 E. Kirkwood Avenue, Bloomington, IN 47405, zaleski@iu.edu. Salary and Rank: $52,000/year, Postdoctoral Fellow Special Instructions: The initial appointment for this position will be for 12 months. Additional 12-month extension will be available based on performance. A competitive salary along with a benefits package will be offered. Interested candidates should submit a cover letter with up to 5-page research proposal maximum , CV, and contact information for three references to https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34697 . Applications will be reviewed upon receipt. \"Indiana University is an equal employment and affirmative action employer and a provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 12/01/2026 Expected Start Date 01/15/2027 Posting Number IU-101744-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34884": {
      "title": "Open Rank Organizations/MHO",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Open Rank Organizations/MHO Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Open Rank Organizations/MHO Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Open Rank Organizations/MHO Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Sociology Location Bloomington Position Summary The Department of Sociology at Indiana University, Bloomington, invites applications for a rank-open (tenured or tenure-track) position beginning in the fall of 2027. We seek an individual with expertise in the sociology of organizations, interpreted broadly, who is committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. We are especially interested in candidates who use innovative methods in their research and can contribute to teaching in the undergraduate Management + Human Organization major that we administer and to substantive and methods training in our graduate program. Ph.D. is required at time of appointment. Applicants should apply online at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/hr/postings/34396 , including a cover letter; CV; statements on research and teaching; 1-3 writing samples; and three letters of reference. Review of applications will begin on October 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Queries can be sent to Art Alderson, Department Chair (aralders@iu.edu), or Andrew Halpern-Manners, Chair of the Personnel Committee (ahm@iu.edu). Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct seriously. Basic Qualifications Ph.D. in Sociology is required at time of appointment. Department Contact for Questions Art Alderson, Department Chair (aralders@iu.edu), or Andrew Halpern-Manners, Chair of the Personnel Committee (ahm@iu.edu). Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 10/16/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101694-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Writing Sample Statement of Research and Teaching List Of References Optional Documents Other Publication 1 Other 2 Other 3 Other 4 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34872": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow - Capone Lab - ENVR",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Postdoctoral Fellow - Capone Lab - ENVR Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Postdoctoral Fellow - Capone Lab - ENVR Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Provide CV, cover letter summarizing research interests and fit for position, writing sample, and a list of three references. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34329 . Posting Details Position Details Title Postdoctoral Fellow - Capone Lab - ENVR Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Environmental and Occupational Health Location Bloomington Position Summary A postdoctoral fellow position is available in the Capone Lab in the Department of Environmental and Occupational Health at the Indiana University School of Public Health-Bloomington. The fellow will join a multidisciplinary team conducting a five-year CDC -funded study focused on developing and applying integrated surveillance approaches for soil-transmitted helminth ( STH ) infection in the southeastern United States. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis, but applications received by October 5, 2026 will be given full consideration, and the search will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. The earliest anticipated start date is October 19, 2026. Dr. Drew Capone’s research group ( https://caponelab.publichealth.indiana.edu ) has broad interests in environmental health microbiology. Current projects include public health surveillance using fecal waste streams, microbial fate and transport, the role of infrastructure in interrupting enteric pathogen transmission, and predicting public health outcomes using quantitative microbial risk assessment. Lab members conduct field research in Mozambique and Indiana, as well as wet lab work in Bloomington, Indiana. We use tools from engineering, epidemiology, and environmental health microbiology to investigate the problems affecting low-income individuals and aim to improve public health in the communities where these people live. Basic Qualifications The postdoctoral fellow position requires a PhD in environmental health, environmental engineering, environmental science, microbiology, or a related scientific field by the time of appointment. We are looking for candidates with experience in several of the following areas (prior experience with helminths is not required): Experience with project management Experience with molecular microbiology methods (e.g., nucleic acid extraction, qPCR, dPCR) and quantitative data analysis Fieldwork experience, including environmental sampling Strong written and oral communication skills An interest in mentoring undergraduate, master’s, and Ph.D. students Department Contact for Questions Questions pertaining to the PeopleAdmin application procedure may be directed to dwarcher@iu.edu . Questions regarding the position may be directed to Dr. Capone at dscapone@iu.edu Additional Qualifications This position offers a unique opportunity to work at the intersection of environmental microbiology, parasitology, epidemiology, and public health surveillance. The project integrates human and environmental samples (i.e., wastewater, septage, soil, flies, and stool) and uses microscopy and molecular methods, including digital PCR , to investigate STH infection and transmission. The fellow will play a leading scientific role in the project while also coordinating laboratory activities and helping manage this large, collaborative study. The fellow will have opportunities to lead studies and peer-reviewed publications, develop and optimize laboratory methods, analyze complex environmental and epidemiologic data, mentor students, and develop independent research questions and proposals. The position includes collaboration with microbiologists, virologists, environmental engineers, entomologists, biologists, and epidemiologists, as well as travel to study sites in Virginia and Alabama. Opportunities may also be available to participate in other domestic and international projects in the Capone Lab. We are particularly interested in candidates who want to develop an independent research profile in environmental health microbiology and who enjoy working across laboratory, field, and quantitative research. Resources are available for conference travel, and the fellow will have access to formal training in grant writing, research ethics, rigor and reproducibility, and research management. Salary and Rank Special Instructions Provide CV, cover letter summarizing research interests and fit for position, writing sample, and a list of three references. Interested candidates should submit applications at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34329 . For Best Consideration Date 10/05/2026 Expected Start Date 10/19/2026 Posting Number IU-101679-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Other Other 2 Other 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34871": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Scientist",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Research Scientist Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Research Scientist Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Research Scientist Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Public & Environmental Affairs Location Bloomington Position Summary The Observing Civic Engagement Lab seeks an Assistant Research Scientist to lead and manage the lab and personnel while conducting original, independent research and creative activity under the direction of a tenured faculty member. What goes on inside community organizations—the religious congregations, service clubs, arts groups, advocacy organizations, and hobby groups that permeate communities? Our lab uses an innovative technique known as systematic social observation ( SSO ) to collect detailed data on what happens at meetings, events, and activities held by community organizations. Analyses of these data will improve understanding of how community organizations work and will help local leaders foster a lively, thriving community. Location: Bloomington, Indiana Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications received by November 20, 2026, will be receive full consideration . To apply, please submit a letter of application, CV, and contact information for up to three references to https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34818 . Basic Qualifications Required: PhD in relevant field ( ABD candidates will not be considered) At least one year of successful postdoctoral research experience Familiarity with systematic social observation methodology Experience working in a research lab Department Contact for Questions Questions regarding the position or application process can be directed to: Professor Matthew Baggetta baggettm@iu.edu, O’Neill School of Public & Environmental Affairs, Bloomington, Indiana. Additional Qualifications Preferred: Project Management certification ( PMP or CMP ) Experience managing large numbers of research assistants Track record of applying for and receiving academic research grants Experience with research budgeting and grant administration Experience with community-engaged research Salary and Rank Commensurate with experience, Assistant Research Scientist. Full benefits included. Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 11/20/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101762-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Writing Sample Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34870": {
      "title": "Associate Vice Provost for Academic Success",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Associate Vice Provost for Academic Success Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Associate Vice Provost for Academic Success Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All tenure-track and non-tenure track faculty are encouraged to apply. To apply: please submit CV, letter of application, and list of at least 3 references. To ensure consideration, applications should be received by November 9, 2026, however the search will continue, and the applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should review the position requirements and apply at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34695 H-1B visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Posting Details Position Details Title Associate Vice Provost for Academic Success Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Undergraduate Education Location Bloomington Position Summary The Office of the Vice Provost for Undergraduate Education ( VPUE ) at Indiana University Bloomington invites applications and nominations for the position of Associate Vice Provost for Academic Success . Reporting to the Vice Provost for Undergraduate Education, the Associate Vice Provost for Academic Success will provide campus-wide leadership for strategies, programs, and partnerships that strengthen undergraduate academic success, persistence, and degree progress. The Associate Vice Provost will lead one of VPUE’s four strategic focus areas and work across academic schools, the College, Enrollment Management, Student Life, University Student Success, faculty governance, and other campus partners to identify and address barriers to undergraduate academic success. The position will provide strategic leadership for a portfolio that includes campus-wide academic advising, retention and persistence, academic recovery and student standing, first-year and other critical-transition academic initiatives, and emerging academic-success priorities . The position is anticipated to begin January 1, 2027, and will carry a 50% administrative appointment in the Office of the Vice Provost for Undergraduate Education and a 50% faculty appointment in the successful candidate’s home academic unit . The Associate Vice Provost reports directly to the Vice Provost for Undergraduate Education and serves as a member of the VPUE senior leadership team. Key Responsibilities The Associate Vice Provost for Academic Success will: Provide strategic leadership for undergraduate academic success initiatives across IU Bloomington. Lead and coordinate campus-wide academic advising in partnership with academic schools and advising leadership. Advance strategies to strengthen undergraduate retention, persistence, academic progress, and degree completion. Provide senior leadership for academic recovery, student standing, and related policies and interventions. Strengthen academic-success strategies for first-year students and students navigating other critical transitions. Identify systemic barriers to undergraduate academic success and convene appropriate campus partners to develop and implement solutions. Use institutional data and evidence to identify student-success challenges, assess interventions, and inform priorities. Foster collaboration among academic schools, the College, Enrollment Management, Student Life, University Student Success, faculty, and other campus partners. Provide strategic leadership and coordination for VPUE units and programs within the Academic Success focus area. Support the development of scalable, evidence-informed approaches to academic support and student success. Represent VPUE on campus and university committees and initiatives related to undergraduate academic success. Advise the Vice Provost for Undergraduate Education on emerging challenges, opportunities, policies, and priorities affecting undergraduate academic success. Undertake additional strategic initiatives as assigned by the Vice Provost. Leadership Scope The Associate Vice Provost will provide senior leadership for an emerging Academic Success portfolio that currently encompasses or connects with: Undergraduate Academic Advising Retention and Persistence Academic Recovery and Student Standing First-Year Academic Success Academic transitions and student mobility Identification and resolution of institutional barriers to undergraduate academic success Emerging campus-wide academic-success initiatives The precise portfolio may evolve as VPUE continues to align its organization and programs with campus priorities. Basic Qualifications Required Qualifications Candidates must: Currently hold a full-time faculty appointment at Indiana University Bloomington and be eligible to maintain a 50% faculty appointment in the candidate’s home academic unit. Have a record of successful academic leadership and service. Demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate education and student academic success. Have experience working collaboratively across academic or administrative boundaries. Demonstrate the ability to build partnerships and lead complex initiatives involving multiple stakeholders. Have excellent communication, judgment, and interpersonal skills. Demonstrate a commitment to evidence-informed decision-making and continuous improvement. Department Contact for Questions Christy Moore Executive Administrative Assistant to the Vice Provost cmgallag@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Strong candidates may also demonstrate: Experience in academic administration or faculty leadership. Experience with undergraduate curriculum, advising, student success, retention, or related areas. Experience leading campus-wide or cross-school initiatives. Understanding of the structures, policies, and academic culture of Indiana University Bloomington. Experience using institutional data to inform academic strategy and decision-making. Demonstrated ability to translate broad institutional priorities into effective programs, policies, or organizational change. Salary and Rank Special Instructions All tenure-track and non-tenure track faculty are encouraged to apply. To apply: please submit CV, letter of application, and list of at least 3 references. To ensure consideration, applications should be received by November 9, 2026, however the search will continue, and the applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should review the position requirements and apply at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34695 H-1B visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. For Best Consideration Date 11/09/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101761-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34866": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Music (Bassoon); Tenure or Tenure-track position (faculty)",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Music (Bassoon); Tenure or Tenure-track position (faculty) Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Music (Bassoon); Tenure or Tenure-track position (faculty) Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. A complete application consists of a letter of application, curriculum vitae, and information about three professional references. You will be asked to provide the name, title, e-mail address, and other information for each of your reference providers. For candidates who advance in this search, an email message with instructions about uploading letters of reference will be sent automatically to each of your provided references. Candidates who advance in this search may also be asked to provide audio/video recordings. Please do not send audio/video files or other materials until requested to do so. If you need help completing your application, contact Rachel Patrick, (812) 855-5541, rnpatric@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Deadline: Applications received by September 26, 2026 will be assured full consideration, however the search will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Music (Bassoon); Tenure or Tenure-track position (faculty) Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Woodwinds Location Bloomington Position Summary The Jacobs School of Music seeks candidates for a position in the Woodwind Department in Bassoon. The ideal candidate will have recognition both nationally and internationally as a performer and as a pedagogue in a wide variety of settings. Primary responsibilities include building and maintaining a studio of undergraduate- and graduate-level bassoon students, teaching studio classes and reed making classes, and coaching chamber ensembles. Additional duties could include teaching orchestra literature classes, pedagogy classes, and other related courses. The successful candidate is expected to participate in departmental meetings, recruitment activities and auditions, doctoral committees, and recital hearing committees, along with other department activities, such as faculty recitals and outreach activities, master classes, service on Jacobs School of Music committees, and other similar activities. Basic Qualifications The ideal candidate must have an established or growing reputation with broad professional experience and have the ability to work successfully with gifted and advanced university-level students. Master’s degree in music is required, or an equivalent of outstanding professional experience will also be considered. Department Contact for Questions Rachel Patrick, Office of the Executive Associate Dean: (812) 855-5541; rnpatric@iu.edu Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Salary and rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Special Instructions A complete application consists of a letter of application, curriculum vitae, and information about three professional references. You will be asked to provide the name, title, e-mail address, and other information for each of your reference providers. For candidates who advance in this search, an email message with instructions about uploading letters of reference will be sent automatically to each of your provided references. Candidates who advance in this search may also be asked to provide audio/video recordings. Please do not send audio/video files or other materials until requested to do so. If you need help completing your application, contact Rachel Patrick, (812) 855-5541, rnpatric@iu.edu . Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. Deadline: Applications received by September 26, 2026 will be assured full consideration, however the search will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. For Best Consideration Date 09/26/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101645-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34857": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor positions, Kelley School of Business (Operations and Decision Technologies, Information Systems)",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant/Associate/Full Professor positions, Kelley School of Business (Operations and Decision Technologies, Information Systems) Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant/Associate/Full Professor positions, Kelley School of Business (Operations and Decision Technologies, Information Systems) Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. To ensure consideration, applications should be received by September 25, 2026; however, the search will continue, and the applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Interested applicants should review the position requirements and apply at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33748. Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant/Associate/Full Professor positions, Kelley School of Business (Operations and Decision Technologies, Information Systems) Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Bloomington Operations and Decision Technologies Location Bloomington Position Summary The Operations and Decision Technologies ( ODT ) Department at the Kelley School of Business, Indiana University Bloomington, invites applicants for multiple tenured/tenure-track positions in Information Systems to begin fall 2027. We welcome applications from individuals with research interests in the broad domains of information systems, software development, data analytics, cybersecurity, IT in organizations, and policies/applications for AI in organizations. Likely teaching responsibilities involve strategy and organizational use of information systems, cybersecurity, management/development/application of AI, applications of modern digital tools for organizations and/or programming and modeling in environments such as Python, R, and SQL . Teaching may include undergraduate, masters, and doctoral level classes. Basic Qualifications Candidates at the entry level must have completed all requirements for a Ph.D. degree, or have completed all but dissertation, in the area of information systems or in a related field and have a strong commitment to excellence in scholarly research and teaching. Candidates at the advanced assistant, associate or full professor level must have a Ph.D. in the area of information systems or in a related field and have a record of high-quality publications, as well as demonstrated teaching experience. While the positions are open rank, pre-tenure candidates are preferred. Department Contact for Questions Candidates should direct any questions to Claire Tafoya at odt@iu.edu. Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Before a conditional offer of employment with tenure is finalized, candidates will be asked to disclose any pending investigations or previous findings of sexual or professional misconduct. They will also be required to authorize an inquiry by Indiana University Bloomington with all current and former employers along these lines. The relevance of information disclosed or ascertained in the context of this process to a candidate’s eligibility for hire will be evaluated by Indiana University Bloomington on a case-by-case basis. Applicants should be aware, however, that Indiana University Bloomington takes the matters of sexual and professional misconduct very seriously. To ensure consideration, applications should be received by September 25, 2026; however, the search will continue, and the applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Interested applicants should review the position requirements and apply at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33748. For Best Consideration Date 09/25/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101606-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Research and Teaching Research Paper/Publication/Writing Sample Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Ability Research Paper 1 Research Paper 2 Research Paper 3 Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
