    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34841": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow, Biology Landeta Lab",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Postdoctoral Fellow, Biology Landeta Lab Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Postdoctoral Fellow, Biology Landeta Lab Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Postdoctoral Fellow, Biology Landeta Lab Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Biology Location Bloomington Position Summary The department of Biology is a large, unified department with strong undergraduate degrees, nationally-ranked graduate programs, and world-class research spanning the breadth of biological questions and experimental systems – from ecosystems to microbiology and developmental biology, from evolution to cell biology, from molecular biology to systems biology, bioinformatics, and genomics. It is always an exciting time for Biology – enormous advances in global genome analysis coupled with unprecedented developments in interdisciplinary research have made the 21st century the Century of Biology. For more information about the department, you can find it here: About: Department of Biology: Indiana University Bloomington. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Landeta Lab in the Department of Biology at Indiana University, Bloomington is seeking a Postdoctoral Fellow. Our department is a large, unified department with world-class research spanning all levels of biological organization and diverse experimental systems. Our lab in Microbiology investigates the processes that take place in the bacterial cell envelope with emphasis into oxidative protein folding. The overarching goal for this position is to make timely progress on our NIH and CFF grants ( https://reporter.nih.gov/search/kpoQKsh8Pkqp4S1_RS1-PQ/project-details/11259946 ), which looks for fundamental insights into novel oxidative reactions, the exported proteins that depend on disulfide bonds, the substrate specificity among thiol-disulfide oxidoreductases and finding novel inhibitors against oxidative folding. We are excited about science and looking for another positive, curious person to join our team. Core topics to work on: (1) In vitro assays to determine inhibitor efficacy against redox membrane proteins (2) Cysteine enrichment of DsbA substrates in E. coli and Mycobacteria using proteomics. (3) determine differences between DsbA proteins of two model organisms, E. coli and M. smegmatis (4) Establishing termini restraining for inhibitor-protein crystallography in collaboration with Prof. Weikai Li. Other general responsibilities include: Supervising undergrads; managing general lab operations; writing up research (e.g. for our annual reports or for manuscripts); presenting findings at lab meetings, microphiles, retreats and conferences; and participating in lab meetings. Basic Qualifications Education and Experience Required: PhD Qualifications: Highly motivated candidates with a Ph.D., in microbiology, biochemistry, biology, or a related field, with a strong interest in studying oxidative protein folding in bacteria and targeting this process in pathogens. High degree of initiative, time management and professionalism, very organized and detail-oriented with proficient communication skills, written and oral and ability to work effectively as a team. Experience with microbial genetics, protein purification, in vitro assays, molecular biology, proteomics is desirable. Trainees will receive health insurance as well as a stipend commensurate with experience. To apply, please submit (1) a cover letter describing your research and educational background, your career goals, why you are interested in this position, and the date you are available to start, (2) a CV highlighting your publications including a brief description of the main findings and how you contributed to the work, and (3) the names and contact info of three references. This can be submitted at the following link: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33897 . Department Contact for Questions For questions about the position, contact Cristina (clandeta@iu.edu). Timing and Compensation: Review of applicants will begin asap and continue until the position is filled. Ideal start date is Oct 1, 2026. The initial appointment is for 1 year, and reappointment for up to 3 years is contingent upon satisfactory performance. Salary will be commensurate with experience, and full benefits are included. The best consideration date is 09/22. Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 09/22/2026 Expected Start Date Posting Number IU-101616-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34825": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Position Experimental Long-Baseline Neutrino Oscillation Physics Indiana University",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Post-Doctoral Position Experimental Long-Baseline Neutrino Oscillation Physics Indiana University Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Post-Doctoral Position Experimental Long-Baseline Neutrino Oscillation Physics Indiana University Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Post-Doctoral Position Experimental Long-Baseline Neutrino Oscillation Physics Indiana University Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Physics Location Bloomington Position Summary Post-Doctoral Position Experimental Long-Baseline Neutrino Oscillation Physics Indiana University The High Energy Neutrino and Particle Astrophysics group at Indiana University is seeking applicants for a post-doctoral position. Our group has leading roles in NOvA operations and data analysis and DUNE construction and data analysis. Indiana University is a center for event reconstruction and data analysis for both NOvA and DUNE , as well as DUNE near and far detector prototyping, and IU hosts a Charge Readout Plane fabrication facility for DUNE’s vertical-drift Far Detector module. At IU, Professors Messier and Urheim are members of NOvA; Professors Messier, Urheim, and Mohayai are members of DUNE . The successful applicant will be expected to be based at Indiana University, Bloomington, and play a leading role in NOvA data analysis and to DUNE analysis or hardware development. A Ph.D. in Physics is required. The position is available for a flexible start date as early as January 1, 2027. We will begin reviewing applications on November 23, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. The appointment will initially be for one year, with the possibility of extension for up to an additional two years. More information about the group and the IU Physics Department can be found at: https://physics.indiana.edu/ Applications, including a curriculum vita and three letters of reference, should be submitted through the application portal located at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34763 . Informal inquiries may be made with Prof. Mark Messier ( messier@iu.edu ), Indiana University, Physics Department, 727 E. Third St., Bloomington, IN, 47405, 812-855-1247. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here, which includes contact information. Basic Qualifications A Ph.D. in Physics is required. Department Contact for Questions Informal inquiries may be made with Prof. Mark Messier ( messier@iu.edu ), Indiana University, Physics Department, 727 E. Third St., Bloomington, IN, 47405, 812-855-1247. Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date 11/23/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101751-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34824": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Lecturer Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Lecturer Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please submit (1) a cover letter describing your experience, educational background, and reasons for interest in the position; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) evidence of teaching ability; (4) a statement of teaching philosophy, and (5) the names and contact information for three letters of references. Application materials may be submitted via( https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34736 ). Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications received by November 23, 2026, will receive full consideration. The search will remain open until the position is filled. H-1B sponsorship is not available for this position. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Posting Details Position Details Title Lecturer Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Biology Location Bloomington Position Summary The Department of Biology in the College of Arts and Sciences at Indiana University invites applicants to fill a full-time non-tenure track Lecturer position beginning August 1, 2027. Responsibilities include teaching four courses a year: a 300-level Genetics lecture in both semesters, and 1-2 additional courses in an area appropriate to the candidate’s expertise but which could include a 100-level introductory majors course focusing on molecular biology. Basic Qualifications A Ph.D. in a biological discipline is desirable, and MS is required. Postdoctoral training or teaching experience may be considered but is not required. Department Contact for Questions Questions about the position should be addressed to Laura Hurley (bioact@iu.edu). Additional Qualifications Candidates should have strong communication and organizational skills, and documented evidence of classroom and/or laboratory teaching ability. Salary and Rank Salary is commensurate with experience and full benefits are included. Special Instructions To apply, please submit (1) a cover letter describing your experience, educational background, and reasons for interest in the position; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) evidence of teaching ability; (4) a statement of teaching philosophy, and (5) the names and contact information for three letters of references. Application materials may be submitted via( https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34736 ). Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications received by November 23, 2026, will receive full consideration. The search will remain open until the position is filled. H-1B sponsorship is not available for this position. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. For Best Consideration Date 11/23/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101755-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Evidence of Teaching Ability Statement of Teaching Philosophy List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
